  {
    "id": "b601da26-a12d-4a58-9dcf-3839bc2c0ed9",
    "title": "Into the Fray",
    "slug": "into-the-fray",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>While Wolfpack grenades are a fast way to kill Leapers, they require looting. This guide provides an alternative strategy utilizing a specific choke point in the Spaceport area, allowing for consistent Leaper kills with less reliance on specific gear, and aiding in quest completion.</p><h2>Step 1: Locate the South Trench Tower</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/into-the-fray_0_00-20.jpg\" alt=\"Map Location: South Trench Tower\"></p><ul><li>Head to the Spaceport area on the map.</li><li>Locate the <strong>South Trench Tower</strong>, which is situated near the 'The Trench' landmark. This tower has multiple broken windows that serve as entry and choke points.</li></ul><h2>Step 2: Access the Tower via Zipline</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/into-the-fray_1_00-27.jpg\" alt=\"Zipline Tower Entry\"></p><ul><li>The most efficient way to get into the tower is by using a zipline.</li><li>Approach the tower from the lower ground and look for an active zipline leading up to one of the broken windows.</li><li>Utilize the zipline to quickly ascend and enter the tower through a broken window. This entry method provides an early warning system and positions you strategically.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Set Up Your Choke Point</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/into-the-fray_2_00-38.jpg\" alt=\"Placing Mines for Defense\"></p><ul><li>Once inside, position yourself facing the broken window where you entered. This window will act as your primary choke point.</li><li><strong>Optional:</strong> Place mines near the zipline entry point on the rooftop. This prevents other players from easily flanking you if they attempt to use the same zipline.</li><li>The Leaper's only other way to reach you in this spot is via a key, making it a highly defensible position against both AI and potentially other players.</li></ul><h2>Step 4: Engage the Leaper</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/into-the-fray_4_00-49.jpg\" alt=\"Leaper Stuck in Choke Point\"></p><ul><li>The Leaper will eventually approach the tower and attempt to enter through the broken window.</li><li>As it tries to squeeze through the opening, it will become an easy target. Focus your fire on its visible weak spots.</li><li>Maintain your position, using the wall as cover if necessary, and continue to shoot until the Leaper is destroyed.</li></ul><h2>Step 5: Collect Leaper Parts &amp; Complete Quests</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/into-the-fray_3_00-43.jpg\" alt=\"Acquiring Leaper Parts\"></p><ul><li>After successfully destroying the Leaper, collect its remains.</li><li>You will often find valuable <strong>Leaper Parts</strong>, which are essential for various quests in Arc Raiders.</li><li>This method is highly effective for quickly completing quests like 'Destroy a Leaper' due to the predictable nature of the fight in this location.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/into-the-fray_5_00-51.jpg\" alt=\"Quest Completion Confirmation\"></p>",
    "summary": "This guide details an easy and repeatable method to eliminate Leapers in Arc Raiders, focusing on a specific choke point location. This strategy is perfect for farming Leaper parts for quests without relying on Wolfpack grenades.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/into-the-fray_4_00-49.jpg",
    "author": "All4nDev",
    "type": "quest",
    "objectives": [
      "Destroy a Leaper",
      "Obtain a Leaper Pulse Unit"
    ],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [
      {
        "id": "b907281a-f19a-4d2d-8a9b-ae0a28ad617b",
