  {
    "id": "c1409478-cf99-4490-9348-3164d69f253c",
    "title": "Arc Survival Guide",
    "slug": "arc-survival-guide",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>The PVE threats in ARC Raiders are numerous and can be deadly if you're unprepared. This guide will walk you through the best ways to take on each type of ARC enemy, focusing on both easy and resource-efficient methods. We'll cover Hornets, Leapers, Rocketeers, ARC Surveyors, and Bombardiers, excluding the Queen as she deserves her own dedicated guide.</p><h2>Step 1: Hornets</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_1_00-34.jpg\" alt=\"Hornet Enemy Overview\"></p><ul><li><strong>Threat Level:</strong> High</li><li><strong>Armor Plate:</strong> Semi Plated</li><li><strong>Primary Attack:</strong> Electric shock</li><li><strong>Special Abilities:</strong> Stuns</li><li><strong>Weakness:</strong> Rear thrusters</li><li><strong>Health:</strong> 200</li></ul><p>Killing a Hornet is like taking down a wasp: aim for the rotors. The front two rotors are armor-plated, so heavy ammo weapons will be more effective against them. If using light ammo, focus on the rear two rotors, though this can be tricky due to the angle.</p><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_4_01-10.jpg\" alt=\"Targeting Hornet Rear Thrusters\"></p><h3>Dodge Attacks:</h3><ul><li>Wait for the three yellow targeting lasers to combine into one.</li><li>They will flash red just before firing, which is your cue to perform a dodge roll.</li><li>Timing is key; spamming dodge roll is ineffective as they compensate.</li><li>A little distance can help, as closer attacks are harder to dodge.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_5_01-21.jpg\" alt=\"Executing a Dodge Roll\"></p><h2>Step 2: Leapers</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_6_01-38.jpg\" alt=\"Leaper Enemy Overview\"></p><ul><li><strong>Threat Level:</strong> Critical</li><li><strong>Armor Plate:</strong> Full Plated</li><li><strong>Primary Attack:</strong> Leaps on you</li><li><strong>Special Abilities:</strong> Releases kinetic energy</li><li><strong>Weakness:</strong> Joints and its eye</li><li><strong>Health:</strong> 1500</li></ul><p>Leapers are vulnerable to tight spaces and fire. Blaze Grenades and Fireball Burners are viable choices.</p><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_7_01-48.jpg\" alt=\"Leaper: Recommended Fire Items\"></p><h3>Method 1: Grenades and Positioning</h3><ul><li>Bring about three Blaze Grenades or Fireball Burners.</li><li>Position yourself in buildings or bunkers where Leapers struggle to get through small doorways or reach you when indoors. For example, using bunkers on the Spaceport is always advised.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_8_01-59.jpg\" alt=\"Utilizing Cover Against Leaper\"></li><li>Aim to land grenades on the center eye-piece of the Leaper to spread fire to all three limbs.</li></ul><h3>Method 2 (Preferred): Blaze Grenade Trap &amp; Jolt Mine</h3><ul><li>This method is easier and more resource-efficient.</li><li>A single Blaze Grenade Trap will shred a Leaper's armor.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_10_02-28.jpg\" alt=\"Leaper: Recommended Trap Items\"></li><li>Place a Blaze Grenade Trap, shoot the Leaper until it launches itself into the air, then take a few steps back.</li><li>Optionally, combine with a Jolt Mine for extra insurance to stun and keep the Leaper in the fire.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_12_02-58.jpg\" alt=\"Combining Blaze Grenade Trap and Jolt Mine\"></li><li>You can recycle Leaper Pulse Units for Advanced Mechanical Components as they're not often useful.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_11_02-32.jpg\" alt=\"Recycling Leaper Pulse Unit\"></li></ul><h2>Step 3: Rocketeers</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_13_03-27.jpg\" alt=\"Rocketeer Enemy Overview\"></p><ul><li><strong>Threat Level:</strong> Critical</li><li><strong>Armor Plate:</strong> Full Plated</li><li><strong>Primary Attack:</strong> Missile Barrage</li><li><strong>Weakness:</strong> Thrusters (covered in armor plating)</li><li><strong>Health:</strong> 1100</li></ul><p>Rocketeers can be terrifying, but easy to defeat with the right strategy.</p><h3>Recommended Weapon: Anvil</h3><ul><li>Anvil (Hand Cannon) is an easy-to-get heavy ammo weapon with a quick fire rate.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_14_03-45.jpg\" alt=\"Rocketeer: Recommended Weapon - Anvil\"></li><li>Approximately 40 rounds of heavy ammo should suffice.</li><li>Consider upgrading your Anvil to increase its fire rate.</li></ul><h3>Strategy: Distance and Thruster Focus</h3><ul><li>Before engaging, ensure you have ample cover, preferably inside a building or close to an entrance.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_17_04-22.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging Rocketeer from Cover\"></li><li>Start your attack from as far away as possible.</li><li>Aim for a single thruster. Taking out two thrusters will send the Rocketeer plummeting to the ground, often killing it outright if high enough.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_16_03-59.jpg\" alt=\"Targeting Rocketeer Thrusters\"></li><li>Rocketeers are slow for a flying ARC, allowing you to kill them before they close distance.</li><li>Wolfpacks are highly effective but generally better saved for Queen fights.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_18_05-11.jpg\" alt=\"Rocketeer: Wolfpack Grenade Option\"></li></ul><h2>Step 4: ARC Surveyor</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_19_05-28.jpg\" alt=\"ARC Surveyor Enemy Overview\"></p><ul><li><strong>Threat Level:</strong> Low</li><li><strong>Armor Plate:</strong> Full Plated</li><li><strong>Primary Attack:</strong> Charges at Raider when provoked</li><li><strong>Weakness:</strong> Exposes its core when transmitting</li><li><strong>Health:</strong> Unknown</li></ul><p>Surveyors are frustrating to chase. This method ensures a solo kill every time.</p><h3>Recommended Items: Showstopper &amp; Trigger 'Nades</h3><ul><li>You'll need one Showstopper grenade (looted, not crafted) and three Trigger 'Nades (craftable).</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_21_05-54.jpg\" alt=\"Surveyor: Recommended Grenades\"></li></ul><h3>Strategy: Stun and Detonate</h3><ul><li>Sneak close enough to land a Showstopper grenade as your opening attack.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_22_06-12.jpg\" alt=\"Stunning and Damaging Surveyor\"></li><li>As soon as the Surveyor is stunned, switch to Trigger 'Nades and lay them on thick. Use all grenades while it's stunned.</li><li>Detonate all three Trigger 'Nades. This should be more than enough to destroy it.</li><li>If no Showstoppers are available, you might still land a couple of Trigger 'Nades before it flees, then finish it off with shots.</li><li>Bring a heavy ammo weapon like the Anvil for best impact if going without Showstoppers.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_23_06-51.jpg\" alt=\"Anvil for Surveyor's Armor\"></li><li>Loot any pieces that fall off the Surveyor, as they may contain valuable ARC Notion Cores.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_24_06-55.jpg\" alt=\"Looting ARC Notion Core\"></li></ul><h2>Step 5: Bastion</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_25_07-02.jpg\" alt=\"Bastion Enemy Overview\"></p><ul><li><strong>Threat Level:</strong> Critical</li><li><strong>Armor Plate:</strong> Full Plated</li><li><strong>Primary Attack:</strong> Projectile</li><li><strong>Weakness:</strong> Rear plate, joints</li><li><strong>Health:</strong> ~2000</li></ul><p>The easiest method for Bastion requires teamwork.</p><h3>Method 1 (Preferred - Team): Torrente &amp; Ammo</h3><ul><li>You'll need a friend (or someone you can tolerate), a Torrente LMG, and a lot of medium ammo.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_26_07-13.jpg\" alt=\"Bastion: Recommended Weapon - Torrente\"></li><li><strong>Setup:</strong> You and your partner should be on either side of the Bastion, with ample cover, preferably on raised ground.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_29_07-41.jpg\" alt=\"Team Strategy Against Bastion\"></li><li><strong>Execution:</strong> Your friend fires the first shot to bait the Bastion's attention. Then, crouch to increase accuracy and aim for the small yellow canister on the rear armor plating.</li><li>Empty your magazine into its back while it's turned. This spot is unarmored.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_29_07-41.jpg\" alt=\"Team Strategy Against Bastion\"></li><li>Step back, reload, and wait for your friend to pull its attention again, then repeat.</li><li>You should kill it within three reloads of a Torrente.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_30_08-01.jpg\" alt=\"Torrente Loadout for Bastion\"></li></ul><h3>Method 2 (Solo): Explosives</h3><ul><li>If solo, bring five or six Trigger 'Nades, Snap Blasts, or Heavy Fuse grenades.</li><li>Stick them to the Bastion itself each time its aim resets.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_31_08-46.jpg\" alt=\"Solo Strategy: Trigger Nade on Bastion\"></li><li>Trying to take down a Bastion solo with basic weaponry by shooting its knee joints is very risky and time-consuming, likely drawing hostile Raiders. Investing in explosives is better.</li></ul><h2>Step 6: Bombardier</h2><ul><li><strong>Threat Level:</strong> Critical</li><li><strong>Armor Plate:</strong> None</li><li><strong>Primary Attack:</strong> Mortar Round</li><li><strong>Special Abilities:</strong> Releases Kinetic Energy</li><li><strong>Weakness:</strong> Rear plate, joints</li><li><strong>Health:</strong> Unknown</li></ul><p>The Bombardier is lethal, with no armor plating on its main body, but its mortar fire is devastating.</p><h3>Method 1 (Preferred - Solo): Trigger 'Nades &amp; Shelter</h3><ul><li>You'll need five or six Trigger 'Nades.</li><li>Find a position to start throwing these grenades from while having a roof over your head. This makes it harder for the Bombardier to land shots.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_35_10-07.jpg\" alt=\"Bombardier Mortar Fire from Cover\"></li><li>Stick as many grenades as possible before it starts opening fire on you.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_34_09-55.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging Bombardier with Trigger Nades\"></li><li>You can ignore the Spotter drones if you have overhead shelter.</li><li>Optionally, bring a Showstopper grenade to lock them in place for easier hits with Trigger 'Nades.</li><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_36_10-33.jpg\" alt=\"Solo Bombardier Takedown from Shelter\"></li><li>Investing in explosives is highly recommended for a quick solo kill.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_37_11-11.jpg\" alt=\"Bombardier: Grenade Preparation\"></li></ul><h3>Method 2 (Team): Distraction &amp; Damage</h3><ul><li>Similar to the Bastion strategy, you need a friend willing to take its attention.</li><li>While your friend distracts, focus your damage on the unarmored rear canister.</li><li>Both players will need a sheltered building on either side of the Bombardier to make this work, which can be very specific and awkward to pull off.</li><li>[SCREENSHOT:10:47]</li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide provides detailed strategies and insights into effectively defeating various ARC enemies in the game. Learn about each enemy's weaknesses, recommended weaponry, and tactical approaches to ensure survival and success.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_6_01-38.jpg",
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-10T09:00:55.384479+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "3942e4c4-c536-4f53-a0a6-53b28807a2c8",
    "title": "ARC Weaknesses",
    "slug": "arc-weaknessess",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>Understanding the unique weaknesses of each ARC enemy type can significantly improve your combat effectiveness. This guide breaks down specific strategies and preferred gadgets for neutralizing Leapers, Rocketeers, Bombadiers, Bastions, Wasps, and Hornets.</p><h2>Step 1: Leaper - Fire Weakness</h2><p>Leapers are highly susceptible to fire damage, which can quickly disable them.</p><ul><li>When encountering a Leaper, prepare to use fire-based consumables. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_0_00-03.jpg\" alt=\"Leaper Introduction\"></li><li>Select either a Blaze Grenade or a Blaze Rod from your inventory. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_1_00-09.jpg\" alt=\"Selecting Blaze Grenade\"></li><li>Throw the fire explosive at the Leaper. The fire will cause significant damage and often make the Leaper fall to the ground. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_2_00-48.jpg\" alt=\"Leaper on Fire\"></li><li>If it stands in the fire too long, it will be temporarily disabled and eventually destroyed. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_3_01-10.jpg\" alt=\"Leaper Disabled\"></li></ul><p><strong>Recommended:</strong> Blaze Grenades or Blaze Rods are very effective against Leapers. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_4_01-25.jpg\" alt=\"Leaper Fire Weakness\"></p><h2>Step 2: Rocketeer - Stun &amp; Target or Heavy Weapons</h2><p>Rocketeers can be tricky due to their aerial mobility, but they have distinct vulnerabilities.</p><ul><li>When a Rocketeer appears, prepare a stunning explosive like a Hornet Driver or Showstopper Grenade. </li><li>Throw the stunning explosive at the Rocketeer to bring it down to the ground. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_6_01-39.jpg\" alt=\"Stunned Rocketeer\"></li><li>Once stunned, you have a 10-second window to get on top of the Rocketeer and shoot its thrusters for maximum damage. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_7_01-46.jpg\" alt=\"Riding the Rocketeer\"></li><li>Alternatively, for a quick and quiet takedown, use high-damage weapons like the Wolfpack or a Holecracker shot. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_8_02-49.jpg\" alt=\"Heavy Weapon Takedown\"></li></ul><p><strong>Recommended:</strong> Hornet Driver, Showstopper Grenade (for stun) or Wolfpack, Ferro Shots to the rotors (for direct damage). <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_9_03-02.jpg\" alt=\"Rocketeer Weaknesses\"></p><h2>Step 3: Bombadier &amp; Bastion - Sticky Explosives or Knee Disabling</h2><p>Both Bombadiers and Bastions share similar weaknesses, particularly to sticky explosives and specific tactical targeting.</p><ul><li>Aim for the weak spot on their back. If you can get close enough without being aggroed, sticky grenades are ideal. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_10_03-17.jpg\" alt=\"Bombadier Weak Spot\"></li><li>Use Snap Blast Grenades or Trigger Nades, which adhere to the enemy and deal explosive damage. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_11_03-43.jpg\" alt=\"Sticky Grenade Hit\"></li><li>Another strategy involves damaging their knees. Continuously shoot their knees until they explode. This will temporarily disable them. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_12_04-15.jpg\" alt=\"Disabling Knees\"></li><li>During the disabled state, unleash as much damage as possible with your weapons. They will not attack you during this brief window.</li><li>In scenarios with multiple ARC types, use Lure Grenades to make Bombadiers or Bastions fire their missiles at other ARC enemies, effectively making them fight each other. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_13_05-01.jpg\" alt=\"Lure Grenade in Action\"></li></ul><p><strong>Recommended:</strong> Snap Blast Grenades, Trigger Nades, and Lure Grenades.</p><h2>Step 4: Wasp - Direct Body Shots</h2><p>Wasps, while less threatening, can be aggressive and annoying. A direct approach is often best.</p><ul><li>If you spot a Wasp in the air and it's about to aggro on you, aim for its main body. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_15_05-33.jpg\" alt=\"Wasp Introduction\"></li><li>Shooting its main body is the most effective way to take it down quickly (e.g., three Anvil shots are typically enough). <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_17_06-21.jpg\" alt=\"Targeting Wasp's Body\"></li><li>Avoid shooting its thrusters, as this will destabilize it and make it fly around unpredictably, making it harder to hit while it continues to attack. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_16_06-07.jpg\" alt=\"Erratic Wasp\"></li></ul><h2>Step 5: Hornet - Front Plating Exploitation</h2><p>Hornets can be taken down efficiently by focusing on their armor plating.</p><ul><li>When engaging a Hornet, instead of trying to hit the smaller back thrusters, focus on shooting the front plating. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_18_06-45.jpg\" alt=\"Hornet Introduction\"></li><li>Once the front plating is shot down, it will expose the thruster directly behind it. Continue to fire through this opening. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_19_07-11.jpg\" alt=\"Shooting Hornet Plating\"></li><li>This method allows you to hit two thrusters on one side with sustained fire, bringing the Hornet down much faster.</li></ul><p>There are many effective ways to deal with ARC enemies, utilizing both your weapons and various gadgets available in the game. Experiment with different strategies, including the use of Horned Drivers or Wasp Drivers, to find what works best for you in different combat scenarios. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_20_07-20.jpg\" alt=\"General Gadget Use\"></p><p>These specialized tools, whether crafted or found, can be highly effective against ARCs, offering creative solutions beyond standard weapon fire. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_21_07-44.jpg\" alt=\"Another Gadget Use\"></p>",
    "summary": "This guide outlines effective strategies and specific weaknesses for various ARC enemies encountered in the game, helping you take them down efficiently.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/arc-weaknesses_5_01-33.jpg",
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-06T14:01:19.407877+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "aa55694a-b071-427a-8ead-0400cfec9e38",
    "title": "Blue Gate Puzzles & Loot",
    "slug": "blue-gate-puzzles-loot",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>This guide will walk you through all the puzzles in the Blue Gate area, covering both surface and tunnel locations. Each puzzle requires specific actions, like inserting batteries or pressing buttons in a sequence, to unlock valuable loot. Pay close attention to map markers and environmental clues to find these elusive objectives.</p><h2>Step 1: Ancient Fort Puzzles</h2><p>The first set of puzzles is located at the Ancient Fort. You'll need to find and insert three batteries into power stations to activate the loot. The batteries typically spawn on crates around the ruins.</p><ul><li>Locate the Ancient Fort on your map. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_0_00-20.jpg\" alt=\"Ancient Fort Map Location\"></li><li>Start at the bottom-left corner of the fort ruins. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_1_00-45.jpg\" alt=\"First Battery Location\"></li><li>Pick up the first battery, usually found on crates. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_1_00-45.jpg\" alt=\"First Battery Location\"></li><li>Head towards the first power station, following the black wires if needed. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_2_01-24.jpg\" alt=\"First Power Station\"></li><li>Insert the battery into the power station. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_3_01-26.jpg\" alt=\"Inserting First Battery\"></li><li>Move to the second ruin building. [SCREENSHOT:01:45]</li><li>Find the second battery on a crate within these ruins. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_4_01-48.jpg\" alt=\"Second Battery Location\"></li><li>Head to the second power station located along the wall, following the black wire. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_5_02-20.jpg\" alt=\"Second Power Station\"></li><li>Insert the second battery. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_6_03-03.jpg\" alt=\"Inserting Second Battery\"></li><li>Go to the third power station, typically in the top floor. [SCREENSHOT:03:07]</li><li>Find the third battery, often in a dark room on a crate. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_7_03-12.jpg\" alt=\"Third Battery Location (Dark Room)\"></li><li>Insert the third battery into the power station. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_8_03-36.jpg\" alt=\"Inserting Third Battery\"></li><li>Once all three batteries are inserted, the lights will turn green, indicating the loot is accessible in the basement. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_9_03-50.jpg\" alt=\"Lights Turned Green\"></li><li>Descend into the basement to collect your loot, usually found on a table or shelf. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_10_03-55.jpg\" alt=\"Ancient Fort Basement Loot\"></li></ul><h2>Step 2: Raider's Refuge Puzzles</h2><p>This location is known as a 'hot drop' due to high player traffic. Exercise caution. You need to press four hidden buttons to unlock the basement loot.</p><ul><li>Locate Raider's Refuge on your map, near 'The Forest' region. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_11_04-02.jpg\" alt=\"Raider's Refuge Map Location\"></li><li>Find the first button on the left side of the basement entrance, next to an AC unit. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_12_04-25.jpg\" alt=\"First Raider's Refuge Button\"></li><li>Press the button to activate the first light. [SCREENSHOT:04:27]</li><li>Locate the second button, often behind some wooden planks or debris on the right side of the basement entrance. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_13_04-50.jpg\" alt=\"Second Raider's Refuge Button\"></li><li>Press the second button. [SCREENSHOT:04:52]</li><li>Head inside the main building structure and climb the ladder. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_14_05-04.jpg\" alt=\"Climbing Ladder to Third Button\"></li><li>Find the third button on the left side once you reach the top. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_15_05-14.jpg\" alt=\"Third Raider's Refuge Button\"></li><li>Press the third button. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_16_05-54.jpg\" alt=\"Fourth Raider's Refuge Button\"></li><li>The fourth button is located on the opposite side of the building's roof, near the communication tower. [SCREENSHOT:06:00]</li><li>Press the fourth button. [SCREENSHOT:06:12]</li><li>With all four buttons pressed, the lights at the basement entrance will turn green. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_17_06-34.jpg\" alt=\"Raider's Refuge Puzzle Complete\"></li><li>Descend into the basement (Secret Cellar) to collect your high-value loot. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_18_06-37.jpg\" alt=\"Raider's Refuge Loot\"></li></ul><h2>Step 3: MANTIKOR (ARC Husk) Puzzles</h2><p>There are two MANTIKOR locations on the map, both with similar puzzles involving power cells. This guide shows one version. You need to find and install two power cells into the massive ARC husk.</p><ul><li>Locate the MANTIKOR husk on your map, near 'Checkpoint'. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_19_06-45.jpg\" alt=\"MANTIKOR Husk Map Location\"></li><li>Find power cells scattered around the dead ARC husk, usually on the ground. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_20_06-55.jpg\" alt=\"Collecting Power Cells\"></li><li>Collect at least two power cells. [SCREENSHOT:07:00]</li><li>Climb up the side of the husk to the interior. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_21_07-15.jpg\" alt=\"Climbing ARC Husk\"></li><li>Locate the first power cell slot and interact to insert a cell. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_22_07-24.jpg\" alt=\"Inserting First Power Cell\"> This will trigger fire and loud noises, alerting other players.</li><li>Jump or climb to the opposite side to find the second power cell slot. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_23_07-33.jpg\" alt=\"Inserting Second Power Cell\"></li><li>Insert the second power cell. [SCREENSHOT:07:38]</li><li>This completes the puzzle, opening a loot container near the power cell slots. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_24_08-05.jpg\" alt=\"MANTIKOR Loot\"></li></ul><h2>Step 4: Reinforced Reception Tunnel Puzzles</h2><p>This puzzle is located within the tunnels, requiring you to follow colored lines and insert batteries. The batteries can sometimes glitch, so be patient.</p><ul><li>Locate the Reinforced Reception area on your map. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_25_08-16.jpg\" alt=\"Reinforced Reception Map Location\"></li><li>Enter the facility and find the main puzzle console. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_26_08-46.jpg\" alt=\"Reinforced Reception Console\"></li><li>Interact with the console; it will show a color (red, blue, or yellow) corresponding to lines on the floor. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_27_08-52.jpg\" alt=\"Console Indicating Yellow\"></li><li>Follow the indicated colored line to a specific door. [SCREENSHOT:09:00]</li><li>Find a battery located near the door you followed. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_28_09-05.jpg\" alt=\"First Battery in Reinforced Reception\"></li><li>Insert the battery into the corresponding slot near the door. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_29_09-09.jpg\" alt=\"Inserting First Battery in Reinforced Reception\"></li><li>Continue following the colored lines and repeating this process. There are typically three batteries to find.</li><li>Sometimes the batteries may be slightly glitched or hidden. Check corners, stairs, and small alcoves. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_30_09-37.jpg\" alt=\"Another Battery Location\"></li><li>After inserting all batteries, return to the main console area. A door will unlock, leading to the loot room. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_33_10-42.jpg\" alt=\"Reinforced Reception Loot Room Open\"></li><li>Collect your loot, which often includes weapon crates and other valuables. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_34_10-45.jpg\" alt=\"Loot in Reinforced Reception\"></li></ul><h2>Step 5: Traffic Tunnel Puzzles</h2><p>Another tunnel puzzle, similar to the Reinforced Reception, but potentially more combat-heavy.</p><ul><li>Locate the 'Traffic Tunnel' on your map, often indicated by a supply beacon. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_35_11-15.jpg\" alt=\"Traffic Tunnel Map Location\"></li><li>Follow the colored lines (red, blue, yellow) on the floor, similar to the previous tunnel puzzle. [SCREENSHOT:11:30]</li><li>Interact with the console to reveal the color sequence. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_36_11-34.jpg\" alt=\"Traffic Tunnel Console\"></li><li>Follow the yellow line down the zipline. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_37_11-44.jpg\" alt=\"Taking Zipline Down\"></li><li>Locate and insert the batteries into their designated slots along the path. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_38_11-50.jpg\" alt=\"Battery Location in Traffic Tunnel\"></li><li>Be aware of potential enemy encounters, as this area can be noisy and attract attention. [SCREENSHOT:11:55]</li><li>Once all batteries are in place, the path to the loot room will be open. [SCREENSHOT:12:05]</li><li>Collect your rewards from the weapon crates and other containers. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_39_12-07.jpg\" alt=\"Traffic Tunnel Loot\"></li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide details all puzzle locations and how to solve them in the Blue Gate area of Arc Raiders, including surface ruins and underground tunnels, to maximize your loot.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/blue-gate-puzzles-loot_34_10-45.jpg",
    "author": "",
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-06T14:26:05.862123+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "0616d22c-f4db-4131-9f1d-19fed06e7230",
    "title": "Cash Farming Guide for Expedition",
    "slug": "cash-farming-guide-for-expedition",
    "content": "<h2>Overview: Expedition Requirements</h2><p>To maximize skill points for your next Raider in the upcoming expedition (deadline December 22nd), you need to accumulate 5 million in stash value. This guide provides strategies to achieve that goal quickly by both minimizing losses and maximizing gains.</p><h2>Minimizing Losses</h2><p>Before focusing on making money, it's crucial to understand how to stop losing it. Every item used or lost in a raid represents a decrease in your overall stash value.</p><h3>Avoid Overspending on Raids</h3><ul><li>Every bullet fired, every bandage used, and every broken shield costs money. Going into a raid with expensive gear means a higher potential loss if you die or use up your supplies.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Run with minimal loadouts:</strong> Start with a basic or 'free' loadout. If you extract successfully, you've gained resources without risking your valuable stash. If you die, the loss is negligible.</li></ul><h3>Rethink Weapon Crafting &amp; Upgrades</h3><ul><li>Crafting weapons and fitting them with attachments actually diminishes their overall value compared to the raw crafting materials.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Sell crafting materials directly:</strong> The base materials required to craft weapons and attachments are often worth more than the completed items. Avoid crafting unless you specifically need the item for a run.</li></ul><h3>Beware of Resource Sinks</h3><ul><li>Certain activities and enemies can be massive drains on your resources with minimal reward.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Avoid the Queen and Matriarch:</strong> These enemies require a significant amount of ammo and medical supplies to defeat. The loot they drop often doesn't justify the resources expended.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Approach PvP strategically:</strong> If you engage in player-versus-player combat with an expensive loadout, you risk losing substantial value. Consider running cheaper loadouts for PvP encounters to minimize potential losses.</li></ul><h2>Maximizing Gains</h2><p>Once you've minimized your losses, you can focus on efficient money-making strategies.</p><h3>Stella Montis Runs</h3><ul><li>Stella Montis is an excellent choice for consistent profit due to its constant availability and high-value loot containers.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Target specific areas:</strong> Focus on the Assembly Workshop, Medical Research, and Lobby areas.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Loot containers:</strong> Search all containers in these high-density loot zones. You can quickly accumulate 50-80k in value within a few minutes.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Minimal entry:</strong> Go in with just a hatch key in your safe pocket to minimize risk. If you die, you've only lost a couple of minutes of your time. If you extract, you have a backpack full of items to sell.</li></ul><h3>Lush Blooms Event</h3><ul><li>This event spawns fruit baskets around the map, offering significant value that can stack in your inventory.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Find locations:</strong> Use online maps like Metaforge to identify fruit basket spawn locations, especially on larger maps like Spaceport.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Collect fruit:</strong> Fruit items stack, allowing you to carry a large amount of value per run.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Be cautious:</strong> Lush Blooms can attract other players, making it a riskier play than Stella Montis.</li></ul><h3>Queen Harvester (Specific Strategy)</h3><ul><li>While fighting the Queen directly is generally inefficient, a specific strategy can yield profit.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Low loadout approach:</strong> Go in with a cheap loadout to minimize risk.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Target the harvester puzzle:</strong> Complete the Queen Harvester puzzle and loot the breachable containers inside. These often contain ARC parts and energy ammo.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Shoot legs and escape:</strong> If you have time and the Queen is not heavily contested, you can shoot off her legs for additional loot, then wait for her to de-aggro and escape via a nearby Raider hatch (Dam Battlegrounds is a good spot for this).</li></ul><h3>High-Density Loot Locations (Day Raids)</h3><ul><li>Certain buildings across various maps are packed with containers, providing consistent value.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Dam Battlegrounds:</strong> Focus on Research &amp; Administration for many lootable containers.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Spaceport:</strong> The Departure Building and Arrival Building have multiple floors filled with containers for quick looting.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Buried City:</strong> The Plaza Rosa area, Grandioso Apartments, Space Travel, and Research buildings are excellent for finding abundant loot.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Utilize Day Raids:</strong> Running these maps during the day often has less competition from other players who might be focused on night raids for rare blueprints.</li></ul><h3>ElectroMagnetic Storm Event</h3><ul><li>During an electrostorm, ARC Husks and Probes appear, offering decent loot with less player competition.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Loot ARC Husks and Probes:</strong> These yield ARC parts and other valuable components.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Spaceport Advantage:</strong> Spaceport is often ideal due to the large, open areas where these spawns typically occur.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Metaphorge map:</strong> Use online tools like the Metaphorge map to identify the spawn locations for ARC Husks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Consistent profit:</strong> Depending on luck, you can make 80-100k per run, potentially 200-300k/hour if you get rare drops like Rocketeer Drivers.</li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide details efficient methods to accumulate wealth in Arc Raiders, focusing on maximizing profit and minimizing losses, essential for the upcoming expedition.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://img.youtube.com/vi/katMeet1A-w/maxresdefault.jpg",
    "author": "All4nDev",
