  {
    "id": "7a7a5bda-ac1d-4a13-84b5-bca6922a4230",
    "title": "Easy coin farm using spotters",
    "slug": "easy-coin-farm-using-spotters",
    "content": "<p>You can easily farm a ton of cash by allowing a bombardier spawn spotters. They spawn infinitely as long as you dont kill him, and their relays are worth 5000 each!</p>",
    "summary": "Spotters are spawned by the bombardier",
    "thumbnail_url": null,
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-04T12:46:09.113617+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "38bce844-e4a1-4f52-939e-3b67d98ca119",
    "title": "Glitched Queen Insta-Kill",
    "slug": "glitched-queen-insta-kill",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>This guide will walk you through the fastest method to defeat the 'Queen' boss netting you a massive 48,000 XP per kill. The strategy relies on precise placement of Blaze Grenade Traps and an Anvil weapon for easily shooting them. While possible solo, it's safer with a teammate to guard against third parties.</p><h2>Step 1: Preparation</h2><ul><li>You will need two Blaze Grenade Traps for this method. Ensure they are the 'Traps' and not regular 'Grenades'.</li><li>Blaze Grenade Traps can be found during free loadout runs or by surrendering repeatedly until you acquire them.</li><li>It's highly recommended to bring a Raider's Key, as it helps with extraction.</li><li>Playing in a duo or trio is advised to protect against other players, as solo runs can easily be third-partied.</li></ul><h2>Step 2: Locating the Queen</h2><p>The Queen can be found on any map, but this guide demonstrates the process on the Blue Gate map. It's crucial to identify the Queen's location early in your raid.</p><ul><li>Open your map to locate the Queen's general area. Look for 'Harvester' on your map. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_3_00-32.jpg\" alt=\"Map Location - Blue Gate\"></li><li>Navigate towards the Queen's location, being mindful of your surroundings and potential enemy players.</li><li>As you approach, observe the Queen's movement. It typically rotates in a circular pattern.</li><li>The primary threat around the Queen is often the 'Rocketeer', so ensure it's not directly in your path or moving away.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Approaching and Placing Traps</h2><p>The key to this strategy is to approach the Queen without aggroing it and correctly placing your traps.</p><ul><li>Approach the Queen from behind or a side where it won't detect you. Since it rotates, you can usually stay out of its line of sight. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_8_01-34.jpg\" alt=\"Approaching Queen from Behind\"></li><li>Eliminate any nearby Wasps (flying drones) that could compromise your stealth. A suppressed weapon is recommended. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_9_01-43.jpg\" alt=\"Shooting a Wasp\"></li><li>Locate the specific weak spot on the underside of the Queen's body. You'll want to place the traps directly into this area.</li><li>Put your Blaze Grenade Traps into your quick-use slots for easy access. Consider moving them to your 'Safe Pocket' in case you die, to retain them.</li><li>Carefully climb up to the Queen's body. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_13_02-37.jpg\" alt=\"Climbing to Queen's Underbelly\"></li><li>Place the first Blaze Grenade Trap so it is lodged inside the Queen's body, not falling to the ground. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_14_02-42.jpg\" alt=\"Placing First Trap\"></li><li>Place a second Blaze Grenade Trap in the same manner. This ensures maximum damage and a one-shot kill.</li></ul><h2>Step 4: Executing the Kill</h2><p>Once the traps are placed, a single shot will detonate them and initiate the kill.</p><ul><li>Once both traps are in place, aim your Anvil weapon at the traps and fire. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_14_02-42.jpg\" alt=\"Placing First Trap\"></li><li>The traps will ignite, causing massive damage to the Queen. You will see a large fire and an explosion effect.</li><li>Watch for the XP notification on the left side of your screen, confirming you've received 48,000 XP. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_17_02-57.jpg\" alt=\"Queen Destroyed &amp; XP Gained\"></li></ul><h2>Step 5: Loot and Extraction</h2><p>After successfully taking down the Queen, it's time to collect your rewards and safely extract.</p><ul><li>Approach the fallen Queen and loot all the valuable items from its core. Ensure you loot everything for additional XP.</li><li>Be extremely cautious during looting, as the sound of the Queen's demise will attract other players.</li><li>Head to a nearby extraction point, such as the Checkpoint or Raider's Hatch, depending on your team's key status.</li><li>The guide shows heading to a nearby petrol station to regroup and prepare for extraction.</li><li>Remain vigilant for other players who may be lurking around extraction zones.</li><li>Successfully extract from the raid, securing your XP and valuable loot. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_27_05-45.jpg\" alt=\"Extraction Point Reached\"></li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide shows you how to quickly and easily defeat the 'Queen' boss using Blaze Grenade Traps to gain 48,000 XP in just a few minutes. Learn the optimal placement and strategy to avoid aggro and secure your loot.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/glitched-queen-insta-kill_8_01-34.jpg",
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-12T12:16:39.643633+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "f887696f-e255-48de-83b1-fe8e4b6834e2",
    "title": "Hidden Bunker Event Location Spaceport",
    "slug": "hidden-bunker-event-location-spaceport",
    "content": "<h2>Overview: Hidden Bunker Event</h2><p>The Hidden Bunker event in Spaceport is an ongoing puzzle that requires activating multiple antennas across the map to open a secret bunker. Inside, players can download data from consoles for XP, with a possible deeper puzzle involving coordinated activation.</p><h2>Step 1: Activating the Antennas</h2><p>The first stage of the Hidden Bunker event involves activating four antennas located across the Spaceport map. Each antenna must be activated to successfully open the bunker.</p><ul><li>Locate the bunker entrance, typically in a set location on the map.</li><li>When a match loads with the Hidden Bunker event, four antennas will appear around the map. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_2_00-37.jpg\" alt=\"Antenna Locations Map\"></li><li>It's recommended to start by activating the antennas in the furthest corners of the map and gradually work your way towards the antenna closest to the bunker entrance.</li><li>To activate an antenna, you need to climb to its rooftop. Many antennas are inaccessible without a zipline. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_3_01-17.jpg\" alt=\"Using Zipline to Reach Antenna\"></li><li>Ensure your Utility Bench is upgraded to Level 2 to craft ziplines. You'll need rope for this.</li><li>Once on the roof, locate and activate the data console. [SCREENSHOT:01:23]</li><li>After activating the console, a wave of ARC enemies (wasps, hornets, rocketeers) will spawn. Be prepared with healing items like Wolfpacks. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_4_01-36.jpg\" alt=\"Fighting ARC Enemies at Antenna\"></li><li>Allow the data download to complete, then interact with the console again to finalize the process.</li><li>Repeat this process for all four antennas across the map. Once the last antenna is activated, a message will appear indicating the 'Hidden Bunker is Now Open'. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_5_01-53.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden Bunker Now Open\"></li></ul><h2>Step 2: Accessing the Hidden Bunker</h2><p>Once all four antennas are activated, the hidden bunker entrance will be accessible. To the left of the departure building. A dash to the bunker will be necessary, as other players might also be heading there.</p><ul><li>Head towards the bunker entrance as quickly as possible. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_0_00-47.jpg\" alt=\"Bunker Entrance Overview\"></li><li>Be aware of potential PvP encounters, as multiple players will likely be rushing to the bunker.</li><li>The area around the bunker entrance may be guarded by enemies like Bombardiers and Bastions. One particular Bastion has been observed shooting through walls, which might be a bug. Try to avoid engaging it directly if possible. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_12_06-44.jpg\" alt=\"Bastion Guarding Bunker Entrance\"></li></ul><h2>Step 3: Data Downloads and Potential Secrets</h2><p>Inside the bunker, you'll find a circular layout with several data consoles. Each console offers an XP reward for downloading data, but there's an ongoing community theory about a deeper puzzle.</p><ul><li>Navigate the circular corridors of the bunker. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_8_02-48.jpg\" alt=\"Bunker Layout on Map\"></li><li>There are approximately seven or eight data consoles inside the bunker.</li><li>To start a data download, interact with a console. You must 'Stay close to continue download'. If you move away, the download will fail. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_7_02-37.jpg\" alt=\"Data Console Interaction Inside Bunker\"></li><li>Upon successful completion, the console will briefly display a green light and award you 500 XP. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_9_03-08.jpg\" alt=\"Successful Data Download (Green Light)\"></li><li>If you leave the console before the download is complete, it will get a red light and reset, allowing you to try again. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_10_03-42.jpg\" alt=\"Failed Data Download (Red Light)\"></li><li>**Community Theory:** It is theorized that activating all data consoles simultaneously with multiple players might unlock a secret area or trigger a special event. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_11_03-47.jpg\" alt=\"Players Coordinating Inside Bunker\"></li><li>This requires significant coordination, ideally with 7-8 players, each standing by a console and activating it at the exact same time (e.g., at a specific countdown timer mark). Due to potential glitches or timing issues, this can be challenging to execute.</li></ul><h2>Important Considerations and Tips</h2><ul><li>**Zipline Usage:** Always place ziplines at the very top of buildings to avoid falling. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_13_07-36.jpg\" alt=\"Correct Zipline Placement\"></li><li>**Zipline Collisions:** Avoid riding a zipline if another player is already on it, as collisions can lead to elimination.</li><li>**Bunker Loot:** The bunker contains numerous lootable containers, including weapon and ammo crates.</li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide provides a detailed walkthrough for activating the hidden bunker event in Spaceport, including antenna activation, accessing the bunker, and understanding the data download consoles inside. It also covers tips for dealing with enemies and navigating the environment.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/hidden-bunker-activation_12_06-44.jpg",
    "author": "All4nDev",
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-09T06:39:16.024779+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "26230950-b410-4bc7-b204-66d918cc9b5b",
    "title": "How to beat the Matriarch - NEW BOSS",
    "slug": "how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>The Matriarch is the latest boss in Ark Hunters. It's an aggressive boss with more attack patterns than the Queen, but surprisingly, it seems to have less health, making it defeatable with less ammo if you are prepared. This guide will walk you through the best strategies and loadouts to take it down.</p><h2>Step 1: Recommended Loadout</h2><ul><li><strong>Primary Weapon:</strong> Hullcracker is highly recommended for its damage efficiency. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_2_00-27.jpg\" alt=\"Recommended Weapon: Hullcracker\"></li><li><strong>Ammo:</strong> Bring approximately 140 Hullcracker ammo.</li><li><strong>Shield:</strong> Use a heavy shield. This will reduce your loot space but is crucial for survival.</li><li><strong>Medkits:</strong> Prioritize bringing more medkits than ammo, as the Matriarch's attacks can be very damaging. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_3_00-41.jpg\" alt=\"Healing Items for Survival\"></li><li><strong>Team:</strong> Fighting with a squad is always easier.</li></ul><h2>Step 2: Understanding Matriarch Attack Patterns</h2><h3>Homing Missiles</h3><ul><li>This is the most dangerous attack. The Matriarch constantly fires barrages of fast-moving homing missiles. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_4_01-05.jpg\" alt=\"Homing Missile Attack\"></li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Stand behind any piece of solid cover. Be aware of some AoE damage and that missiles can sometimes curve around corners. Pick your cover wisely to avoid being hit.</li></ul><h3>Gas Mines</h3><ul><li>The Matriarch sends out barrages of gas mines. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_5_01-42.jpg\" alt=\"Gas Mine Deployment\"></li><li>Being in the gas will cause your character to cough uncontrollably, disabling your ability to fire. [SCREENSHOT:01:54]</li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Avoid the gas at all costs. While it doesn't appear to deal direct damage, the debuff is detrimental to combat.</li></ul><h3>Flashbangs</h3><ul><li>The Matriarch can fire flashbang-like projectiles. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_6_01-59.jpg\" alt=\"Flashbang Attack\"></li><li>Standing near these will temporarily blind you, which is not ideal in combat. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_7_02-00.jpg\" alt=\"Flashbang Blindness\"></li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong> If you see one, run away to avoid the blinding effect.</li></ul><h3>Summoned ARC</h3><ul><li>The Matriarch will call in waves of other ARC units.</li><li><strong>Rocketeer:</strong> This is often the main threat among the summoned units and can deal significant damage. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_8_02-20.jpg\" alt=\"Rocketeer Summoned\"></li><li><strong>Bastion:</strong> Bastions can pin you down and prevent you from looting after the Matriarch is defeated. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_9_02-29.jpg\" alt=\"Bastion Threat\"></li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Prioritize eliminating summoned ARC units, especially Rocketeers and Bastions, to prevent being overwhelmed or losing out on loot.</li></ul><h3>Impenetrable Shield</h3><ul><li>The Matriarch periodically deploys a large, impenetrable blue shield. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_10_03-24.jpg\" alt=\"Impenetrable Shield\"></li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong> You cannot damage the Matriarch while this shield is active. Wait until the shield dissipates before resuming your attack.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Combat Strategy</h2><ul><li><strong>Utilizing Cover:</strong> Always prioritize cover to avoid missile barrages and other attacks. Find thick cover that blocks AoE damage and curving projectiles.</li><li><strong>Targeting Weak Points:</strong> The Matriarch's biggest weak point is its red core located in its head. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_11_03-37.jpg\" alt=\"Targeting the Weak Point\"> Consistently shooting the head will expose this core.</li><li>You can also target the legs, which have armor plating, but once that's broken, they take damage quickly.</li><li><strong>Map Choice:</strong> Dam Battlegrounds is generally considered the best map for fighting this boss due to ample cover and strategic positions. Blue Gate is not recommended due to insufficient cover.</li></ul><h2>Step 4: Loot &amp; Rewards</h2><ul><li>The main loot dropped by the Matriarch is the Matriarch Reactor. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_12_04-10.jpg\" alt=\"Matriarch Reactor Loot\"></li><li>This legendary item is used to craft the new Energy Burst Rifle (Battle Rifle).</li><li>Ensure you secure your loot quickly after defeating the Matriarch, as lingering enemy units like Bastions can still pose a threat and prevent collection.</li><li><br></li><li><br></li></ul><p>Credit to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sxr8NWSrrE4\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">The Gaming Merchant</a> for the screenshots used in this guide.</p>",
    "summary": "This guide provides a comprehensive strategy for defeating the Matriarch boss, including recommended loadouts, understanding its attack patterns, identifying weak points, and tips for efficient combat and loot collection.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/how-to-beat-the-matriarch-new-boss_10_03-24.jpg",
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-14T12:56:07.433476+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "22c0dfff-91c5-46c4-af45-615b2c898565",
    "title": "Important Materials and Their Locations",
    "slug": "important-materials-and-their-locations",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>This comprehensive guide details the locations and crafting methods for all crucial items needed for workbench upgrades and expedition progress in Arc Raiders. We'll cover Scrappy items, Gunsmith materials, Gear Bench components, Medical Lab supplies, Refiner resources, Utility Station parts, and Expedition specific items. Theres a cheat sheet list on arcraidersmap.app/materials. Credit to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MgjnW1WF-oQ\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">The Gaming Merchant</a> for putting this video together.</p><h2>Step 1: Scrappy Items</h2><h3>Dog Collar</h3><ul><li>These can be found in any residential container such as wardrobes and drawers.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_0_00-57.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Residential Container for Dog Collar\"> Search residential containers for a good chance to find them.</li></ul><h3>Lemon &amp; Apricot</h3><ul><li>Your best bet for finding lemons and apricots is in the Blue Gate map area.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_1_01-07.jpg\" alt=\"Lemon Location on Blue Gate Map\"> Head to the Olive Grove location on the Blue Gate map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_2_01-11.jpg\" alt=\"Collecting Lemons from a Tree\"> Interact with the lemon trees to kick lemons to the ground for collection.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_3_01-14.jpg\" alt=\"Detailed Map Pin for Olive Grove\"> You can see the Olive Grove location on the map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_4_01-21.jpg\" alt=\"Apricot Tree Area on Blue Gate Map\"> Apricot trees are also found in the same Olive Grove area, as indicated on the map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_5_01-24.jpg\" alt=\"Collecting Apricots from a Tree\"> Interact with the apricot trees to collect the fruit.</li><li>Alternatively, in Buried City, Morano Park, you can also find apricot trees.</li><li>Be cautious, as a Bastion or Bombardier often spawns here.</li></ul><h3>Mushrooms</h3><ul><li>Mushrooms can be found in multiple locations across the Dam Battlegrounds map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_7_01-46.jpg\" alt=\"Mushrooms on Water Treatment Pipes\"> Look for them growing on pipes near the Water Treatment Control building.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_8_01-52.jpg\" alt=\"Mushrooms in Hydroponic Dome Complex\"> They also grow inside the Hydroponic Dome Complex.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_9_01-55.jpg\" alt=\"Mushrooms on a Fallen Tree Log\"> You'll find them growing on trees in the Scrapyard and Wreckage areas.</li><li>For the most consistent mushroom farming, head to the Spaceport map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_10_02-02.jpg\" alt=\"Best Mushroom Farming Spot - Spaceport Map\"> Locate this specific spot near the East Container Yard and Rocket Assembly.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_11_02-04.jpg\" alt=\"Harvesting Guaranteed Mushrooms\"> This area has trees with guaranteed mushroom spawns, making it ideal for farming.</li></ul><h3>Prickly Pear</h3><ul><li>These cacti fruits are found on the ground alongside cacti.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_12_02-22.jpg\" alt=\"Prickly Pear Location - Dam Battlegrounds\"> A good spot on the Dam Battlegrounds map is around Pattern House.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_13_02-32.jpg\" alt=\"Harvesting Prickly Pears from Cacti\"> Look closely among the cacti for the fruits to harvest.</li><li>Alternatively, you can find prickly pears in Buried City.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_14_02-28.jpg\" alt=\"Prickly Pear Location - Buried City Map (Plaza Riva)\"> They are often scattered around the Plaza Riva area.</li></ul><h3>Very Comfortable Pillow &amp; Cat Bed</h3><ul><li>Both of these items are considered residential loot.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_15_02-44.jpg\" alt=\"Searching Residential Cabinet for Pillows/Cat Beds\"> Search wardrobes, drawers, and various containers in residential areas.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_16_02-48.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Residential Shelves for Items\"> Keep searching all residential containers; they may seem rare at first but are plentiful.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_17_02-53.jpg\" alt=\"Buried City Map for Residential Loot\"> For example, in Buried City, loot all buildings in the Plaza Rosa area.</li></ul><h2>Step 2: Gunsmith Items</h2><h3>Rusted Tools &amp; Advanced Mechanical Components</h3><ul><li>These items are frequently found by breaching vehicles.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_18_03-22.jpg\" alt=\"Checkpoint Area for Rusted Tools/Advanced Mechanical Components\"> Head to the Checkpoint and Highway Collapse areas on the Blue Gate map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_19_03-31.jpg\" alt=\"Breaching a Car for Rusted Tools/Advanced Mechanical Components\"> Breach all the abandoned cars in these locations. Rusted Tools are common, and Rusted Gear has a small chance to drop.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_20_03-44.jpg\" alt=\"Breaching Server Cabinet for Advanced Mechanical Components\"> For Advanced Mechanical Components, your best bet is breaching server cabinets found in almost any building across all maps.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_21_04-17.jpg\" alt=\"Rusted Tools Blueprint and Source (Toolbox)\"> For Rusted Tools, look for rusted toolboxes and red lockers in industrial areas.</li></ul><h3>Wasp Driver</h3><ul><li>To acquire a Wasp Driver, you must eliminate a Wasp.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_23_04-23.jpg\" alt=\"Wasp Driver Source (Wasp)\"> Loot the Wasp's body after defeating it.</li></ul><h3>Sentinel Firing Cores</h3><ul><li>Sentinels (the spider-like turrets) drop these.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_24_04-36.jpg\" alt=\"Sentinel Firing Core Location - Research &amp; Administration\"> On the Dam Battlegrounds map during a Night Raid, you'll find a Sentinel at the Research &amp; Administration area, on the blue stairs outside the building.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_25_04-40.jpg\" alt=\"Sentinel Firing Core Location - Control Tower\"> Another Sentinel can be found at The Breach.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_26_04-43.jpg\" alt=\"Sentinel Firing Core Location - The Breach\"> There's often one here as well. Night Raids on Dam Battlegrounds provide the best chance for these drops.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Gear Bench Items</h2><h3>Electrical Components</h3><ul><li>Electrical Components can be crafted using the Refiner if you have the blueprint.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_27_04-57.jpg\" alt=\"Crafting Mechanical Components (Gear Bench)\"> Crafting is often the easiest method, requiring Plastic Parts and Rubber Parts.</li><li>Alternatively, search server cabinets which are abundant across all maps in industrial and electrical zones.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_28_05-05.jpg\" alt=\"Dam Battlegrounds Map for Electrical Components (Server Cabinets)\"> These containers often yield electrical components.</li></ul><h3>Hornet Driver</h3><ul><li>Eliminate a Hornet to obtain a Hornet Driver.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_29_05-10.jpg\" alt=\"Hornet Driver Source (Hornet)\"> Loot its body after defeating it.</li></ul><h3>Power Cables</h3><ul><li>Power Cables can be found in various loot containers.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_30_05-13.jpg\" alt=\"Power Cable Item Image\"> Red lockers, like those found in industrial buildings, are a good source.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_31_05-14.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Red Lockers for Power Cables\"> Looting these containers frequently yields Power Cables.</li></ul><h3>Industrial Batteries</h3><ul><li>Industrial Batteries have a high chance of spawning in industrial areas.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_32_05-20.jpg\" alt=\"Hydroponic Dome Complex for Industrial Batteries\"> The Hydroponic Dome Complex on the Dam Battlegrounds map is an excellent location.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_33_05-27.jpg\" alt=\"Picking up Industrial Battery from Shelf\"> Look specifically on the shelves within this complex for batteries.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_34_05-33.jpg\" alt=\"Blue Gate Map - Headhouse Underground for Batteries\"> You can also find them on shelves within the breachable underground room at the Blue Gate map's Headhouse.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_35_05-36.jpg\" alt=\"Breaching Underground Door for Batteries\"> Breach the large door by inserting three batteries into the console to access the room.</li></ul><h3>Advanced Electrical Components</h3><ul><li>These advanced components can be found or crafted.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_36_05-47.jpg\" alt=\"Ancient Fort Location for Advanced Electrical Components\"> One method is to solve the Ancient Fort puzzle quest on the Blue Gate map, leading you underground to find them.</li><li>Alternatively, head to the Reinforced Reception area on the Blue Gate map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_37_06-01.jpg\" alt=\"Reinforced Reception Puzzle Console\"> Solve the underground puzzle by inserting three batteries to open a large door.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_38_06-09.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Advanced Electrical Components from Computers\"> Inside, you'll find a control room with numerous Advanced Electrical Components on the computers.</li></ul><h3>Bastion Cell</h3><ul><li>Bastion Cells come from Bastions, you should get anywhere from 2-4 per kill. Theres a full arc killing guide <a href=\"https://arcraidersmap.app/guides/arc-survival-guide\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> that explains more strategies to taking all enemies down.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_39_06-15.jpg\" alt=\"Bastion Cell Source (Bastion)\"></li></ul><h2>Step 4: Medical Lab Items</h2><h3>ARC Alloy</h3><ul><li>ARC Alloy is dropped by any defeated ARC enemy.</li><li>Simply eliminate any ARC and loot their remains.</li></ul><h3>Cracked Bioscanners</h3><ul><li>Cracked Bioscanners are often found in medical facilities.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_41_06-28.jpg\" alt=\"Buried City Hospital for Cracked Bioscanners\"> The Hospital in Buried City is a prime location.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_42_06-36.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Cracked Bioscanner from Hospital Bed\"> Look for them frequently spawning on top of the hospital beds rather than inside containers.</li></ul><h3>Durable Cloth</h3><ul><li>Durable Cloth can be found in any container across Arc Raiders.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_44_06-49.jpg\" alt=\"Durable Cloth Crafting Blueprint\"> It's also easily crafted using the Refiner from Fabric.</li></ul><h3>Rusted Shut Medical Kit</h3><ul><li>These kits can be found in pretty much any container.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_45_06-59.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Rusted Shut Medical Kit from Container\"> For a higher chance, search the Hospital in Buried City.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_46_07-05.jpg\" alt=\"Buried City Hospital Map for Medical Kit\"> The Hospital is a good general source for medical supplies.</li></ul><h3>Antiseptic</h3><ul><li>Antiseptic can be found in various containers, especially medical ones.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_47_07-16.jpg\" alt=\"Buried City Plaza Rosa Pharmacy for Antiseptic\"> A consistently great spot is the pharmacy building in Plaza Rosa, Buried City.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_48_07-22.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Antiseptic from Pharmacy Shelves\"> Search the store shelves on the ground floor of this breachable building for a high yield.</li></ul><h3>Surveyor Vault</h3><ul><li>To get a Surveyor Vault, you must track down and defeat a Surveyor.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_49_07-35.jpg\" alt=\"Surveyor in the Sky (Blue Beam)\"> Look for a large blue beam of light in the sky at the start of a match; this indicates a Surveyor's location.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_50_07-40.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging a Surveyor for Loot\"> Bring powerful weapons like a Wolfpack or Showstopper, as Surveyors tend to roll away. Loot it after destruction.</li></ul><h2>Step 5: Refiner Items</h2><h3>ARC Power Cells</h3><ul><li>Any ARC enemy will drop ARC Power Cells upon defeat.</li><li>Simply eliminate and loot ARCs to collect these.</li></ul><h3>Toasters</h3><ul><li>Toasters are typically found in residential areas.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_52_07-54.jpg\" alt=\"Buried City Map for Toasters (Residential)\"> Search any residential container, such as wardrobes and drawers, in locations like Buried City.</li></ul><h3>ARC Motion Cores</h3><ul><li>These cores are dropped only by specific ARC enemies.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_53_08-00.jpg\" alt=\"ARC Motion Core Blueprint\"> They can drop from the Leaper, Queen, Rocketeer, Bastion, or Surveyor.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_54_08-01.jpg\" alt=\"Looting ARC Husk for Motion Cores\"> You can also obtain them by looting ARC husks.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_55_08-14.jpg\" alt=\"Dam Battlegrounds Old Battleground for ARC Husks\"> The Old Battleground area on the Dam Battlegrounds map is a good place to find numerous ARC husks to breach.</li></ul><h3>Bombardier Cell</h3><ul><li>Defeat a Bombardier to acquire a Bombardier Cell.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_56_08-21.jpg\" alt=\"Bombardier Cell Source (Bombardier)\"> Loot its parts after eliminating it.</li></ul><h2>Step 6: Utility Station Items</h2><h3>Damaged Heat Sinks</h3><ul><li>Damaged Heat Sinks are found in server cabinets.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_57_08-27.jpg\" alt=\"Breaching Server Cabinet for Damaged Heat Sinks\"> These cabinets are scattered across all maps in most buildings.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_58_08-35.jpg\" alt=\"Power Generation Complex for Damaged Heat Sinks\"> The Power Generation Complex underground section on the Dam Battlegrounds map is a notable spot.</li></ul><h3>Electrical Components</h3><ul><li>Electrical Components can be crafted at the Refiner using Rubber Parts and Plastic Parts.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_59_08-47.jpg\" alt=\"Crafting Electrical Components\"> Alternatively, you can recycle Wasp or Hornet Drivers to obtain them.</li></ul><h3>Snitch Scanner</h3><ul><li>To get a Snitch Scanner, you must defeat a Snitch.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_60_08-59.jpg\" alt=\"Snitch Scanner Source (Snitch)\"> Snitches are the ARC enemies that emit a large search beam of light. Shoot them three times with an anvil to destroy them, then loot.</li></ul><h3>Fried Motherboards</h3><ul><li>Fried Motherboards are found in electrical containers.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_61_09-07.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Shelves for Fried Motherboards\"> Server cabinets are a common source.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_62_09-18.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Voltage Converter (example for Motherboards)\"> You can also find them on shelves in the underground breachable room within Reinforced Reception on the Blue Gate map.</li></ul><h3>Leaper Pulse Units</h3><ul><li>Eliminate a Leaper enemy to obtain Leaper Pulse Units.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_64_09-27.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Containers for Leaper Pulse Units\"> Loot the Leaper's body after defeating it.</li></ul><h2>Step 7: Expedition Items</h2><h3>Synthesized Fuel</h3><ul><li>Synthesized Fuel can be found in cars and residential loot containers.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_65_09-46.jpg\" alt=\"Purchasing Synthesized Fuel from Celeste\"> For an easier method, visit Celeste at the Traders and purchase them using Assorted Seeds.</li></ul><h3>Crude Explosives &amp; Pop Triggers</h3><ul><li>These items are often found together in explosive-related areas.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_66_09-50.jpg\" alt=\"Tamanish Gun Shop for Explosives/Pop Triggers\"> Eliminate Pops (fireball enemies) and Fireball Burners found underground on any map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_67_10-04.jpg\" alt=\"Reinforced Reception Map for Crude Explosives/Pop Triggers\"> Alternatively, in the Blue Gate map, go underground into the Reinforced Reception area.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_68_10-46.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Shelves for Explosive Compound/Crude Explosives\"> Search the black containers and shelves here for Crude Explosives and Pop Triggers.</li></ul><h3>Laboratory Reagents</h3><ul><li>Laboratory Reagents are rare crafting items.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_69_10-24.jpg\" alt=\"Buried City Plaza Rosa for Laboratory Reagents\"> The pharmacy building in Plaza Rosa, Buried City, on the ground floor shelves, is a reliable place to find them.</li></ul><h3>Explosive Compound</h3><ul><li>Explosive Compound is commonly found in areas with high explosive density.</li><li>[SCREENSHOT:10:34] Head to the underground section of Reinforced Reception on the Blue Gate map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_68_10-46.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Shelves for Explosive Compound/Crude Explosives\"> Search the black containers and shelves within this area for a good chance to find it.</li></ul><h3>Rocketeer Driver</h3><ul><li>Eliminate a Rocketeer to obtain a Rocketeer Driver.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_70_10-55.jpg\" alt=\"Dam Battlegrounds Map for Rocketeer Drivers (ARC Husks)\"> You may also find these by breaching ARC husks in the Old Battleground area on the Dam Battlegrounds map.</li></ul><h3>Steel Springs</h3><ul><li>Many items can be recycled into Steel Springs using the Refiner.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_71_11-15.jpg\" alt=\"Hydroponic Dome Complex for Steel Springs\"> For a direct source, search the Hydroponic Dome Complex on the Dam Battlegrounds map; springs here often spawn in stacks of three.</li></ul><h3>Cooling Fan</h3><ul><li>Cooling Fans are typically found in server cabinets.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_72_11-31.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Server Cabinet for Cooling Fan\"> Breach server cabinets to find them.</li><li>You will also need Wires (from Scrappy), Electrical Components (from Refiner or recycling), and Durable Cloth (from Refiner).</li></ul><h3>Exodus Modules</h3><ul><li>Exodus Modules are specific to the Spaceport map.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_73_11-43.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Rocket Assembly for Exodus Modules\"> Go to the Rocket Assembly area and loot all industrial containers, especially the red lockers.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_74_11-49.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Red Locker for Exodus Modules\"> These red lockers have a decent chance of containing Exodus Modules.</li></ul><h3>Light Bulbs</h3><ul><li>Light Bulbs can be found in practically any loot container.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_75_11-51.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Container for Light Bulbs\"> Simply loot everything you come across, and you'll accumulate them.</li></ul><h3>Sensors</h3><ul><li>Sensors are found in server cabinets.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_76_11-56.jpg\" alt=\"Breaching Server Cabinet for Sensors\"> Breach server cabinets across maps. Refer to the in-game cheat sheet for items that can be recycled into sensors.</li></ul><h3>Batteries</h3><ul><li>Batteries are very common and can be found in most containers.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_77_12-09.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Container for Batteries\"> Loot general containers in any area to find them.</li></ul><h3>Magnetic Accelerators</h3><ul><li>These advanced items can be found in specific industrial locations.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_78_12-15.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Rocket Assembly for Magnetic Accelerators\"> Head to the Rocket Assembly area on the Spaceport map and search its containers.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_79_12-20.jpg\" alt=\"Crafting Magnetic Accelerator\"> Alternatively, if your Refiner is Level 3, you can craft them using Advanced Mechanical Components and ARC Motion Cores.</li></ul><h3>Humidifier</h3><ul><li>The Humidifier is a random loot item.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_80_12-34.jpg\" alt=\"Humidifier in Stash (Random Loot)\"> Search various containers across all maps; it can spawn in any container type.</li></ul><h3>Motor</h3><ul><li>Motors are primarily found by breaching cars.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_81_12-48.jpg\" alt=\"Breaching Car for Motor\"> They have a very low chance, similar to Rusted Gear, but persist in breaching cars in areas like Highway Collapse.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_82_12-54.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Car for Motor\"> Continue breaching cars, and you will eventually find them.</li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide covers essential item locations and crafting recipes for all workbench upgrades and expedition requirements in Arc Raiders, ensuring you know what to keep and where to find it.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/resource-acquisition_21_04-17.jpg",
    "author": "All4nDev",
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-10T05:50:36.867961+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "e47edb2e-503b-46d5-a09d-0659895b1bea",
    "title": "Is the security breach skill worth it?",
    "slug": "is-the-security-breach-skill-worth-it",
    "content": "<h1>\u2694\ufe0f Worth the Points? A Deep Dive into the ARC Raiders Security Breach Skill and Epic Loot Locations</h1><p>In <em>ARC Raiders</em>, the skill tree presents players with tough choices, but few skills are as mysterious\u2014and potentially rewarding\u2014as the <strong>Security Locker Breach Skill</strong>. It demands a significant investment of your limited skill points, making many wonder: is it truly worth sacrificing other crucial upgrades like increased stamina or faster movement?</p><p>The short answer, according to The Gaming Merchant, is a resounding <strong>yes</strong>\u2014the skill is extremely worthwhile, acting as one of the fastest routes to obtaining end-game weaponry.</p><p>Here is a breakdown of the commitment required, the powerful loot you can expect, and a guide to the key security locker locations.</p><h3>The Skill Tree Investment Dilemma</h3><p>Acquiring the Security Locker Breach Skill requires committing a significant portion of your skill points early on.</p><ul><li><strong>The Cost:</strong> Maxing out a single skill tree requires <strong>36 points</strong> (or 36 levels). Since the maximum number of skill points available is only 75, unlocking the breach skill early means you will have to forgo other foundational skills like better stamina and faster movement for a period.</li><li><strong>The Warning:</strong> If you invest in this skill too soon, you will struggle with basic movement, and may need to bring 10 to 15 adrenaline syringes per raid just to compensate for the lack of stamina skills.</li><li><strong>The Long-Term Plan:</strong> The ideal path is to unlock the Security Breach skill and then use the remaining points to pick up the essential stamina skills at the bottom of the other trees, rather than trying to max out another tree entirely.</li></ul><h3>What's Inside? The Epic Loot Breakdown</h3><p>The key to the skill's value is the high-tier, consistent loot found within the security containers. These are essentially weapon lockers that drastically reduce the need for crafting high-level gear.</p><p>Security lockers are consistently filled with:</p><ul><li><strong>Guaranteed High-Tier Weapons:</strong> The weapons found are <em>always</em> Level 2 and you will <strong>never</strong> find common weapons.</li><li><strong>Epic Tier Weapons:</strong> You can expect to find highly desirable epic tier weapons regularly, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Bobcat</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Patina (arguable the best gun in the game)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Tempest</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Volcano shotgun</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Other weapons like the Ventor, Anvil, El Toro, and Torren</li><li><strong>Essential Crafting Components:</strong> The lockers frequently contain parts crucial for upgrading your weapons, such as:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Heavy Gun Parts</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Light Gun Parts</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Complex Gun Parts</li><li><strong>Other Gear:</strong> Grenades, ammo, and valuable blueprints are also part of the loot pool.</li></ul><p><strong>Crucially, the loot pool appears to be consistent across all maps</strong>, meaning no matter where you are, a security locker provides the same chance at great loot. Furthermore, the loot from these security lockers was observed to be <strong>much better</strong> than loot found behind locked doors that require a key.</p><h3>\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f Security Locker Locations Guide</h3><p>The video highlighted several locations where you can consistently find security lockers across different maps:</p><h4>The Dam</h4><ul><li><strong>Breached Room Location:</strong> Look for a breached door in the dam area (this was done on a normal, not night, raid). This spot is considered one of the best in the game for security lockers. The path involves running alongside the top level of the floodgates area, turning right, finding doors leading down to the overlook, sliding down, and opening the drawbridge to cross.</li><li><strong>Power Complex:</strong> In the power generation complex underground, you can find a locker out in the open. This location is riskier as it is a common player area and you don't have to breach a door for cover.</li></ul><h4>Bluegate</h4><ul><li><strong>Under the Church:</strong> There is a security locker that requires you to input four buttons to open the room.</li><li><strong>Underground Area:</strong> Another one is located in the Bluegate underground area, one floor above the Bluegate locked door.</li></ul><h4>Spaceport</h4><ul><li><strong>Locked Bunkers:</strong> Lockers are spread out in the small bunkers across the spaceport. These usually have breachable doors on the outside.</li><li><strong>Tip:</strong> You can often peek through the open window of the bunkers to check if the lockers are inside, saving you the time of breaching the door.</li></ul><h4>Buried City</h4><ul><li><strong>Locked Room:</strong> At least one security locker has been found in a locked room within Buried City.</li></ul><p>The security breach skill is an investment, but the ability to consistently grab Level 2 epic weapons makes it a core component of any loadout focused on end-game progression.</p>",
    "summary": "\"..the skill tree presents players with tough choices, but few skills are as mysterious\u2014and potentially rewarding\u2014as the Security Locker Breach Skill\"",
    "thumbnail_url": null,
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-04T10:13:09.277888+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "40df0f05-5f67-48ae-b5c3-9c270014c261",
    "title": "Paving the Way Quest",
    "slug": "paving-the-way-quest",
    "content": "<p>This guide will walk you through the 'Paving the Way' quest in The Cycle: Frontier, detailing the locations and interactions required to complete the mission.</p><h2>Step 1: Locate an ENELICA Building on Dam Battlegrounds</h2><ul><li>Begin your quest by deploying to the Dam Battlegrounds map.</li><li>Navigate towards the Water Treatment Control building, which is an ENELICA facility.</li><li>Approach the building from the southwest side.</li><li>Look for the ENELICA logo on the wall near the entrance. </li></ul><h2>Step 2: Interact with the Researcher's Notice Board</h2><ul><li>On the wall next to the ENELICA logo, you'll find a notice board.</li><li>Interact with the notice board to collect the researcher's note. This completes the first part of the quest.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Access the Top Floor in Buried City</h2><ul><li>Next, deploy to the Buried City map.</li><li>Locate the Convenio in Piazza Roma. This is identified as a southern building near the Western Station on the map. </li><li>More specifically, you'll be looking for the southern of two adjacent buildings, just northeast of Grandioso Apartments and right next to Western Station. </li><li>Enter this building and find a zip line.</li><li>Use the zip line to ascend to the top floor (Floor 6). </li><li>Upon exiting the zip line, you will be on floor 6 of Apartment Building A1. </li></ul><h2>Step 4: Find and Search the Researcher's Flat</h2><ul><li>Once on the top floor, enter the room with a burning fire and destroyed ARC objects.This will trigger the next quest objective to find research data.</li><li>Proceed into the adjacent room, which serves as the researcher's flat.</li><li>Look for a desk with multiple computer monitors. </li><li>Interact with the computers to search for research data. This will complete the final objective.</li></ul><h2>Step 5: Claim Your Rewards</h2><ul><li>After interacting with the research data, the 'Paving the Way' quest will be complete.</li><li>Return to the quest menu to claim your rewards. </li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide provides a detailed walkthrough for completing the 'Paving the Way' quest in The Cycle: Frontier, covering all objectives across Dam Battlegrounds and Buried City.",
    "thumbnail_url": null,
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:22:30.029888+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "9bade7e7-c611-48f3-9671-92c6c285e9bb",
    "title": "Stella Montis Keys - Where To Use",
    "slug": "stella-montis-keys-where-to-use",
    "content": "<p>where to use the various keys in Stella Montis. Assembly Admin Key, Medical Storage Key, Archives Key, Security Checkpoint Key</p><h2>Assembly Admin Key Door</h2><ul><li>Just Below Assembly Worshops yellow tier area. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_1_00-05.jpg\" alt=\"Map Location of Assembly\"></li><li>Interact with the door to use your Stella Montis Assembly Admin Key and unlock it. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_4_00-24.jpg\" alt=\"Unlocking the Ground Floor Door\"></li></ul><h2><br></h2><h2><br></h2><h2>Medical Storage Key Door</h2><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_1_00-10.jpg\" alt=\"Detailed Starting Point\"></p><p>From your starting point, where you can see the large rocket-like structure, turn around and proceed through the corridor. Follow the path until you reach the 'Medical Research North Wing' entrance.</p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_2_00-18.jpg\" alt=\"Medical Research North Wing Entrance\"></p><p>You will go down a set of stairs and navigate through the open area filled with various equipment and workstations. Continue following the path until you see the door</p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_3_00-25.jpg\" alt=\"Medical Storage Room Door\"></p><p>At this door, you will be prompted to use your Stella Montis Medical Storage Key to unlock it.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><h2>Archives Key Door</h2><ul><li>Make your way down to the Easter section of the Seed Vault</li><li>The destination is within the Eastern Tunnel region of Seed Vault. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_1_00-08.jpg\" alt=\"Map Location: Seed Vault\"></li><li>You will encounter several pipes; climb over them to proceed. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_2_00-15.jpg\" alt=\"Navigating Obstacles: Climbing Pipes\"></li><li>Immediately turn right after climbing the pipes and go all the way down the hall, on the right side is the door</li><li>This is the 'STORAGE ROOM' door, which requires the 'Stella Mantis Archives Key' to unlock. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_3_00-36.jpg\" alt=\"Destination Reached: Archives Door\"></li></ul><p><br></p><h2><br></h2><h2>Security Checkpoint Key Door</h2><ul><li>Open your map and confirm your location in the 'Lobby' section of Stella Montis.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_1_00-09.jpg\" alt=\"Initial Checkpoint View\"></li><li>From the lobby, move past the initial checkpoint structure.</li><li>Turn right immediately after passing the main checkpoint desk.</li><li>Enter the small room located behind the security reception area.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/stella-montis-key-use_3_00-15.jpg\" alt=\"Room Behind Reception\"></li><li><br></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Continue straight through this room, then make another right turn.</li><li>Proceed down the narrow corridor until you reach the end.</li><li>Turn left, then immediately right again.</li><li>The first door on your right is the Stella Montis Security Checkpoint. This is where you will use your key.</li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_3_00-24.jpg\" alt=\"Security Checkpoint Door\"></li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide shows you where to use the various keys in Stella Montis. Assembly Admin Key, Medical Storage Key, Archives Key, Security Checkpoint Key",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/assembly-admin-key-use_4_00-24.jpg",
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-16T12:42:55.001922+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "ffb90cfd-dc37-450e-827f-f1f603ed4d9a",
    "title": "Stella Montis Overview and Looting Guide",
    "slug": "stella-montis-overview-and-looting-guide",
    "content": "<h2>Overview: Stella Montis Map</h2><p>Stella Montis is a new, high-risk, high-reward map in Arc Raiders</p><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_1_00-35.jpg\" alt=\"Stella Montis Ground Floor Map Overview\"></p><h2>Medical Research (Red Tier)</h2><p>The Medical Research area is a Red Tier zone offering significant loot but also high PvP action. Expect frequent player encounters and challenging enemies.</p><ul><li><strong>High PvP Encounters:</strong> You will face aggressive players. Be ready for combat at all times. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_2_00-54.jpg\" alt=\"Entering Medical Research\"></li><li><strong>New ARC: Shredders:</strong> This area introduces new ARC enemies called Shredders. They are dangerous and can quickly deplete your health. Aim for their blue thrusters for critical damage. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_5_03-55.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging Shredder ARCs\"></li><li><strong>Looting Valuable Items:</strong> Look out for trash cans and other containers. They often contain high-value crafting materials and keys, like the Buried City Town Hall Key. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_4_01-53.jpg\" alt=\"Trash Can Loot in Medical Research\"></li><li><strong>Always be Cautious:</strong> Even if players call out as friendly, be wary. Many will attack without warning. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_3_01-05.jpg\" alt=\"Player Ambush in Medical Research\"></li><li><strong>Loot Value:</strong> After 3 successful runs, the total loot value was approximately 208K credits. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_6_05-27.jpg\" alt=\"Medical Research Loot &amp; PvP Rating\"></li></ul><h2>Assembly Workshops (Yellow Tier)</h2><p>Despite being a Yellow Tier area, Assembly Workshops offer surprisingly high-quality loot, making it a very lucrative spot, but also highly contested.</p><ul><li><strong>Epic Rarity Loot:</strong> Expect to find many epic rarity crafting materials and good weapons. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_7_05-50.jpg\" alt=\"Looting in Assembly Workshops\"></li><li><strong>Intense PvP:</strong> This area is a hotspot for player-versus-player combat. Be prepared for constant engagements. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_8_07-00.jpg\" alt=\"Intense PvP in Assembly Workshops\"></li><li><strong>Speeding Up Runs:</strong> Bringing a Radar Hatch key can help you quickly access certain areas and extract faster.</li><li><strong>Loot Value:</strong> After 2 successful runs (before an unfortunate death), the loot value was 172K credits. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_9_10-12.jpg\" alt=\"Assembly Workshops Loot &amp; PvP Rating\"></li></ul><h2>Seed Vault (Red Tier)</h2><p>The Seed Vault is a Red Tier area, but it's unique in its offerings and playstyle.</p><ul><li><strong>Only Seeds:</strong> This area is primarily for collecting seeds, a crafting material for the seed vendor.</li><li><strong>Time-Consuming:</strong> There are over 500 containers, each yielding only a few seeds. It's a slow and tedious process. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_11_10-45.jpg\" alt=\"Tedious Looting in Seed Vault\"></li><li><strong>Low PvP:</strong> Due to the low-value, high-effort loot, players are generally more friendly here, making it a calmer experience. [SCREENSHOT:11:00]</li><li><strong>Overall Assessment:</strong> Not recommended for quick money making. It's more for specific crafting needs or a relaxed vibe. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_12_11-12.jpg\" alt=\"Seed Vault Map Location and Vibes\"></li></ul><h2>Cultural Archives (Red Tier)</h2><p>Cultural Archives is another Red Tier zone, but its loot profile differs from Medical Research.</p><ul><li><strong>Trinkets and Blueprints:</strong> This area mainly offers trinkets and a small chance for blueprints. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_13_11-21.jpg\" alt=\"Cultural Archives Looting\"></li><li><strong>Low Value Loot:</strong> Most containers will yield only fabric and plastic parts, making it less profitable than other Red Tier zones.</li><li><strong>Friendly Encounters:</strong> Similar to the Seed Vault, the low-value loot means less competition, often leading to friendly player interactions. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_14_11-46.jpg\" alt=\"Friendly Encounter in Cultural Archives\"></li></ul><h2>Lobby (Yellow Tier)</h2><p>The Lobby is a Yellow Tier area that can be surprisingly lucrative if you know where to look.</p><ul><li><strong>Mantikor Room:</strong> On Floor 3, the room marked 'Mantikor' is often filled with high-tier loot and fuel canisters. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_16_13-12.jpg\" alt=\"Mantikor Room in Lobby\"></li><li><strong>Strategic Fuel Canister Use:</strong> Fuel canisters can be thrown to create explosions, useful against groups of enemies. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_17_13-30.jpg\" alt=\"Fuel Canister Explosive Use\"></li><li><strong>Overall Assessment:</strong> A great place to stop by for valuable loot if it hasn't been cleared, offering high risk and high reward. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_15_12-48.jpg\" alt=\"Lobby Loot &amp; PvP Rating\"></li></ul><h2>General Stella Montis Strategy</h2><p>Success on Stella Montis requires more than just knowing loot spots; it demands tactical awareness and adaptability.</p><ul><li><strong>PvP Awareness is Key:</strong> This map is a PvP fest. Always be ready for combat, even if players seem friendly.</li><li><strong>Clear the Aggressors:</strong> If you eliminate the aggressive PvP players early in a raid, fewer new players will spawn in, potentially leaving you with a calmer looting experience.</li><li><strong>Spawn Point Strategy:</strong> Unlike other maps, players spawn directly into Point of Interests (POIs) on Stella Montis. This means you need to loot whatever is closest to your spawn quickly before other players get to it. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_18_14-24.jpg\" alt=\"Spawn Point Strategy on Map\"></li><li><strong>High Risk, High Reward:</strong> The best loot is often in the most dangerous areas. Decide if the potential reward is worth the risk.</li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide identifies the most profitable looting zones and key strategies for survival and wealth accumulation on the Stella Montis map in Arc Raiders.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/best-stella-montis-loot_1_00-35.jpg",
    "author": "All4nDev",
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-15T04:17:56.549319+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "5a252ca4-9f64-45b5-8f58-cfd11ab7def7",
    "title": "Stench of Corruption Quest",
    "slug": "stench-of-corruption-quest",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>This guide walks you through the steps to complete \"The Stench of Corruption\" quest, which requires you to navigate the Spaceport map, find a specific key, and use it in the underground tunnels.</p><h2>Step 1: Reach the Departure Building</h2><p>Your first objective is to reach the southwest lobby of the Departure Building. This building is a large, red structure on the map.</p><ul><li>Set a waypoint to the Departure Building on your map.</li><li>Travel to the Departure Building. Consider doing this during a normal raid rather than a Cold Snap raid as you'll be covering a significant distance.</li></ul><h2>Step 2: Find the Staff Locker Room</h2><p>Once you arrive at the Departure Building, you'll need to enter it and locate the staff locker room.</p><ul><li>Head towards the back side of the Departure Building. There are multiple entrances here.</li><li>Enter through one of the openings in the back of the building.</li><li>Inside, navigate towards the northwest side of this back area.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Locate a small door under a staircase that leads into the staff locker room.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><h2>Step 3: Obtain the Flushing Terminal Key</h2><p>The key required for the quest's next step is found within the staff locker room.</p><ul><li>Search the locker room for any clues. There will be various loot items here.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Find the white hazmat suits hanging on a rack in the center of the room. Interact with them to drop the Flushing Terminal Key.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><h2>Step 4: Access the Tunnels and Use the Key</h2><p>With the Flushing Terminal Key in hand, your final task is to reach the underground tunnels and use the key at a specific terminal.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Head towards the underground tunnels. You can use an entrance near the Launch Towers.</li><li>Once inside the tunnels, proceed towards the north-west side.</li><li>Locate a control room with a terminal.</li><li>Interact with the terminal using your Flushing Terminal Key to override the bypass process. This will complete the quest.</li></ul><h2>Quest Completion</h2><p>After successfully using the key at the terminal, the quest will be marked as complete, and you can claim your rewards.</p><p><br></p>",
    "summary": "This guide details how to complete \"The Stench of Corruption\" quest on Spaceport in ARC Raiders, covering key locations and steps to find the Flushing Terminal Key and use it.",
    "thumbnail_url": null,
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2026-01-16T21:59:32.467451+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "904c1e02-4021-41a7-b372-b07fc0cbb35c",
    "title": "Trials 3 Star Guide",
    "slug": "trials-3-star-guide",
    "content": "<h1>Weekly Trials Overview</h1><p>This guide will show you how to three-star all weekly trials in just two matches without extensive preparation or specific blueprints. We'll cover throwing snowballs at Rocketeers, damaging flying ARC enemies, opening ARC probes, destroying fireballs (all on Cold Snap), and dealing damage to Shredders (on Stella Montes Night Raid).</p><h2>Step 1: Throw Snowballs at Rocketeers</h2><p>For a three-star trial, you'll need to throw 16 snowballs at a Rocketeer. Snowballs spawn in clumps around most buildings on all maps. You can collect one snowball, wait two seconds, and collect another from the exact same spot to stack them efficiently.</p><ul><li>Collect 20-25 snowballs before engaging if possible. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_0_00-30.jpg\" alt=\"Collecting Snowballs\"></li><li>Snowballs will respawn after a short delay, allowing you to pick up multiple from a single spot. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_1_00-48.jpg\" alt=\"Snowball Respawn Mechanic\"></li></ul><h3>Bringing Down a Rocketeer</h3><p>Rocketeers are flying enemies, so you need a strategy to ground them:</p><ul><li>**Less Reliable Method:** Use a Showstopper or Hornet Driver to stun it and hope it lands on its back. This method relies heavily on luck and timing. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_3_01-28.jpg\" alt=\"Stunning Rocketeer with Showstopper\"></li><li>**Consistent Method:** Shoot two thrusters on the same side of the Rocketeer. This will disable its flight and bring it to the ground. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_4_01-46.jpg\" alt=\"Shooting Rocketeer Thrusters\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Focus only on the thrusters. Damaging other parts might destroy it before both thrusters are out, making it fly again. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_5_01-53.jpg\" alt=\"Targeting Rocketeer Thrusters\"></li></ul><p>Once grounded, pelt the Rocketeer with snowballs until the trial requirement is met. Each snowball deals 1 damage. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_6_02-22.jpg\" alt=\"Pelting Grounded Rocketeer with Snowballs\"></p><h2>Step 2: Damage Flying ARC Enemies</h2><p>This trial requires damaging flying ARC enemies like Snitches, Wasps, and Hornets.</p><ul><li>Find high ground, such as the Grandioso apartment buildings, for better visibility and engagement. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_7_03-00.jpg\" alt=\"Locating Flying ARC Enemies\"></li><li>Shoot Snitches; they will often spawn waves of Wasps and Hornets, which are flying ARC enemies. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_8_03-15.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging Flying ARC Enemies\"></li><li>You'll encounter another Rocketeer later in the match. Aim to damage its thrusters without killing it if other players are around, so they can also complete their trials.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Open ARC Probes</h2><p>To complete this trial, you need to open and loot three ARC probes.</p><ul><li>Look for smoke plumes rising into the air across the map; these indicate crashed ARC probes. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_9_03-59.jpg\" alt=\"Spotting ARC Probe Smoke\"></li><li>When you get close, probes will appear on your minimap. Regularly open your map to spot them as you traverse the area. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_10_04-24.jpg\" alt=\"ARC Probe on Map\"></li><li>You can loot probes that other players have already breached and opened. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_11_04-36.jpg\" alt=\"Looting an ARC Probe\"></li></ul><h2>Step 4: Destroy Fireballs</h2><p>You'll need to destroy six fireballs for this trial.</p><ul><li>A great location for fireballs on Buried City (Cold Snap) is the underground Metro area. In Cold Snap events, the Metro is open, allowing full access. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_12_04-46.jpg\" alt=\"Destroying Fireballs in Metro\"></li><li>After eliminating fireballs on one side of the Metro, call the train to cross over and find more on the other side. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_13_05-27.jpg\" alt=\"Crossing Metro for Fireballs\"></li><li>Fireballs also spawn in other buildings like the Hospital, Space Travel, Research &amp; Administration, and Galleria. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_14_05-46.jpg\" alt=\"Fireball Spawn Locations\"></li></ul><h2>Step 5: Deal Damage to Shredders</h2><p>This trial is best done on Stella Montes Night Raid, where you only need to eliminate three Shredders (instead of six on a normal day raid).</p><ul><li>**Weapons and Explosives:**</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Two Snapblast grenades or five Impact grenades thrown at the Shredder's bottom can destroy it. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_15_06-05.jpg\" alt=\"Using Grenades on Shredder\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Synthesized Fuel also acts as an effective makeshift explosive and is commonly found in the lobby. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_16_06-50.jpg\" alt=\"Using Synthesized Fuel on Shredder\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Anvil or Il Toro shotgun are effective weapons. Aim for the three thrusters on the Shredder to quickly destroy it. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_17_07-06.jpg\" alt=\"Shooting Shredder Thrusters\"></li><li>**Tactics:** Utilize cover to peek in and out, shooting the Shredder. Retreat behind cover when it's about to fire. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_18_07-34.jpg\" alt=\"Shredder Combat Strategy\"></li><li>**Looting:** Always loot Shredder Gyros, as they are a new requirement for expeditions. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_19_07-29.jpg\" alt=\"Looting Shredder Gyros\"></li><li>**Spawn Locations:** Shredders can be found in the Lobby, Sandbox area, Loading Bay Metro, Cultural Archives, Seed Vault Metro/Escape Area, and between Assembly Workshops and Medical Research. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_20_08-00.jpg\" alt=\"Shredder Spawn Areas\"></li></ul><p><br></p>",
    "summary": null,
    "thumbnail_url": "https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-mastery_3_01-28.jpg",
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fQGKSA4T9l0",
    "created_at": "2025-12-30T09:00:43.42299+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "a7762921-088c-41f7-87f1-822a0fef1de8",
    "title": "Trials High Scoring Guide for Week of Nov 10th",
    "slug": "trials-high-scoring-guide-for-week-of-nov-10th",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>This guide will show you how to get 3 stars on all weekly trials to earn free rewards and blueprints. We'll cover the best strategies for each trial, including optimal routes, enemy weaknesses, and tips for dealing with other players. Credit to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-_uWD-XcJ3U\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">The Gaming Merchant</a> for the tips!</p><h2>Step 1: Damage Bastions</h2><p>For the Damage Bastions trial, you'll need to destroy Bastions found at specific locations. Your goal is to reach one of these locations as quickly as possible so that no other players get there before you. The easiest one to use is the Hydroponic Dome Complex.</p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_0_00-22.jpg\" alt=\"Bastion Spawn Map\"></p><ul><li>**Locate Bastion Spawns:** Identify the Hydroponic Dome Complex or Power Generation Complex on the map as potential Bastion spawn points.</li><li>**Rush to Location:** Head directly to one of the Bastion spawn points. The Hydroponic Dome Complex is often the easiest due to a cheese strategy.</li><li>**Utilize Door Peeking:** Position yourself at one of the Hydroponic Dome doors. Bait the Bastion towards the door. It's too large to get its head around the corner, allowing you to peek and shoot its kneecaps safely.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_1_00-46.jpg\" alt=\"Door Peeking Strategy\"></p><ul><li>**Target Kneecaps:** Focus fire on the yellow kneecaps. Destroying them will temporarily disable the Bastion.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_2_00-59.jpg\" alt=\"Targeting Kneecaps\"></p><ul><li>**Damage During Disable:** When the Bastion is disabled, freely attack it and use any Snapblast grenades or Triggernades for maximum damage.</li><li>**Inventory Check:** Keep an eye on your ammo and other items in your inventory.</li><li>**Destroy Bastion:** Continue this process until the Bastion is destroyed.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_4_01-34.jpg\" alt=\"Destroyed Bastion\"></p><ul><li>**Player Awareness:** Be cautious of other players attempting to PvP you. Consider bringing barricades to protect your back while engaging the Bastion.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_5_01-46.jpg\" alt=\"Barricade for PvP Defense\"></p><ul><li>**Repeat at Pipeline Tower:** After destroying the first Bastion, quickly move to the Pipeline Tower for the second Bastion.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_6_02-06.jpg\" alt=\"Map to Pipeline Tower\"></p><ul><li>**Optimal Strategy at Pipeline Tower:** Use a similar peeking strategy at the Pipeline Tower entrance, as shown. While not as perfect as Hydroponic, the door still provides significant cover.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_7_02-16.jpg\" alt=\"Pipeline Tower Engagement\"></p><ul><li>**Respawn Farming:** Bastions will respawn in the same locations periodically. If you destroy the Hydroponic Dome Bastion fast enough, it will respawn with the next wave, allowing you to repeat the process for more points.</li><li>**Efficient Looting:** Only spend a short time looting after destroying a Bastion. Time is crucial, and other players may be nearby.</li><li>**Maximize Spawns:** As a solo player, aiming for two Bastion destructions will get you three stars. If you want to push further, speed-run the first two and then wait for the next spawn wave to fight one or two more.</li><li>**Time Management:** Always monitor the final extract time. A good rule of thumb is to allow one minute for every 100 meters you need to travel to the extraction point.</li></ul><p>By following these steps, you can achieve a high score in the Damage Bastions trial.</p><h2>Step 2: Damage Wasps</h2><p>The Damage Wasps trial is an excellent opportunity to accumulate a high score, especially during the Spaceport Hidden Bunker event, which offers 2x points.</p><ul><li>**Choose Spaceport Hidden Bunker:** This event is ideal for Wasp farming due to its bonus points and fewer ground-based ARCs.</li><li>**Prepare Snitch Scanners:** Before entering the raid, stock up on Snitch Scanners. Bringing 5 will allow you to kill 10 Wasps for a 3-star rating.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_14_04-36.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Wasp Locations Map\"></p><ul><li>**Engage Wasps Safely:** Upon arrival, use Snitch Scanners one by one to aggro Wasps. Fight them individually to avoid being overwhelmed.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_15_04-39.jpg\" alt=\"Wasp Combat from Cover\"></p><ul><li>**Utilize Cover:** Find a safe position, such as inside a building, to peek out and shoot Wasps.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_16_04-54.jpg\" alt=\"Using Snitch Scanners\"></p><ul><li>**Monitor Scanners:** Keep track of your Snitch Scanners in your inventory.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_17_05-20.jpg\" alt=\"Snitch Scanners in Inventory\"></p><ul><li>**Launch Tower Strategy:** After using your initial Snitch Scanners, head to the Launch Tower. Climb the ladder for an advantageous position.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_18_05-32.jpg\" alt=\"Approaching Launch Tower\"></p><ul><li>**Elevated Position:** The Launch Tower provides a great vantage point, making it difficult for other players to push you while you farm Wasps.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_19_05-37.jpg\" alt=\"Climbing Launch Tower Ladder\"></p><ul><li>**Hidden Bunker Opening:** Once the Hidden Bunker is open, most players will rush there, leaving you with free rein to farm Wasps.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_20_05-46.jpg\" alt=\"Wasp Farming from Launch Tower\"></p><ul><li>**Aggro More Wasps:** If you run out of Snitch Scanners, you can shoot nearby passive snitches to aggro Wasps and Hornets towards you.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_21_06-49.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden Bunker Open Notification\"></p><ul><li>**Wasp Aiming Tip:** Wasps are coded to dodge your aim when you're aiming down sights. Instead, wait for the Wasp to stop moving (usually just before it fires), then aim slightly above its head for a one-shot kill with the Hullcracker.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_22_07-02.jpg\" alt=\"Wasp Aiming Strategy\"></p><ul><li>**Hornet Strategy:** The same aiming tip applies to Hornets.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_23_07-10.jpg\" alt=\"Hornet One-Shot Kill\"></p><ul><li>**Destroy Entire Wasp:** For maximum points, ensure you destroy the Wasp entirely, not just its wings. Three Anvil shots to the body will kill it.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Destroy Fireballs</h2><p>The best map for destroying Fireballs is Dam Battlegrounds at night, particularly the Testing Annex area.</p><ul><li>**Optimal Location:** Head to the Testing Annex on Dam Battlegrounds (Night Raid).</li><li>**Fireball Spawns:** This area is rich with Fireball spawns, particularly in the underground sections and buildings.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_27_08-11.jpg\" alt=\"Fireball Encounter\"></p><ul><li>**Optimal Route:** Start at Water Treatment Control, proceed through the underground to Primary Facility, then Control Tower, and finally Research &amp; Administration. There are many Fireballs in these areas.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_28_08-21.jpg\" alt=\"Destroy Fireballs Trial Progress\"></p><ul><li>**Shooting Fireballs:** Focus on shooting the Fireballs as they appear. They often come in groups.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_29_08-28.jpg\" alt=\"Destroying a Fireball\"></p><ul><li>**Efficient Pathing:** Continue moving through the designated route, destroying Fireballs as they spawn. Once you've cleared the Fireballs in one area, move to the next.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_30_08-40.jpg\" alt=\"Fireball Farming Route (Dam Battlegrounds)\"></p><ul><li>**Keep Moving:** If no more Fireballs are spawning in your current location, proceed to Power Generation Complex or other marked areas, always keeping an eye on the final extract.</li></ul><h2>Step 4: Download Data during Hidden Bunker</h2><p>This trial requires you to download data from PCs within the Hidden Bunker, typically on the Spaceport map.</p><ul><li>**Access Hidden Bunker:** Wait for the Hidden Bunker event to be available. Activate the satellites to open the bunker entrance.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_31_09-16.jpg\" alt=\"Downloading Data from PC\"></p><ul><li>**Locate PCs:** Once inside, find the PCs in the Hidden Bunker. There are generally eight PCs available for data download.</li><li>**Initiate Download:** Interact with a PC to start the data download. You must stay close to the PC for the download to continue.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_33_09-38.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden Bunker Entrance\"></p><ul><li>**Wait for Completion:** Stay near the PC until the download is complete. This process takes some time.</li><li>**Repeat for All PCs:** Download data from all eight PCs to maximize your score (up to 6,400 points).</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_35_09-50.jpg\" alt=\"Data Download Trial Results\"></p><ul><li>**Cooldown Period:** If another player has recently downloaded from a PC, it will be on a short cooldown (1-2 minutes) before you can access it.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_36_10-04.jpg\" alt=\"Other Player Downloading Data\"></p><ul><li>**Solo vs. Squad:** Doing this solo can be boring but is an easy way to get points. In solos, other players are often friendly and will share PCs.</li></ul><h2>Step 5: Deliver Carriables</h2><p>For the Deliver Carriables mission, the most efficient way to collect and deliver carriables is by utilizing Field Depots.</p><ul><li>**Field Depot Locations:** Field Depots are available on Dam Battlegrounds, Buried City, and Spaceport.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_37_10-20.jpg\" alt=\"Delivering Carriable to Field Depot\"></p><ul><li>**Collect Carriables:** Find and collect carriables (e.g., batteries, data drives). You can often find multiple carriables around Field Depots.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_38_10-24.jpg\" alt=\"Carriables in Inventory\"></p><ul><li>**Deliver to Depot:** Drop your collected carriables into the Field Depots. You can deposit more than one carriable in each depot.</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/max-weekly-trial-stars_39_10-37.jpg\" alt=\"Field Depot Locations Map (Spaceport)\"></p><ul><li>**Maximize Deliveries:** Aim to deliver four batteries in a Night Raid to achieve the full three stars for this trial.</li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide provides expert strategies and optimal routes to achieve 3-star ratings on all weekly trials in the game, focusing on maximizing points for Bastions, Wasps, Fireballs, and data downloads.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://img.youtube.com/vi/-_uWD-XcJ3U/maxresdefault.jpg",
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-11T11:36:30.016881+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "3dee99df-885c-43c1-9d88-fd059897d206",
    "title": "Trials Week 5",
    "slug": "trials-week-5",
    "content": "<h2>Overview: Maximize Your Trial Points</h2><p>For all trial challenges, aim to complete them during major map conditions like Night Raids, Electromagnetic Storms, or the Hidden Bunker event, which offer a 2x bonus on your UI. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_0_01-06.jpg\" alt=\"Map Selection for Bonus Points\"> Always load into a fresh map to maximize your time, keeping an eye on the timer at the top of your screen. If you're in at the 30-40 minute mark, you'll maximize points. Staying in the round until the last minutes and extracting after most players have left can often be safer when playing solo. Remember, you must successfully extract to retain any points earned.</p><h2>Trial 1: Damage Rocketeers</h2><p>This challenge pushes both solo players and teams to deal as much damage as possible to Rocketeers in a single raid. Full points are awarded if you or your team are the sole ones damaging a Rocketeer until it's brought down. Consider using a combination of Wolfpacks, Hullcrackers, Jupiters, and Heavy Ammo based weapons for maximum efficiency.</p><ul><li>A full kill of a Rocketeer is worth about 2600 points. You'll need two kills to hit the three-star threshold. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_10_02-34.jpg\" alt=\"Points for a Rocketeer Kill\"></li><li><strong>Farming Location 1: Spaceport Launch Tower</strong></li><li>Anchor yourself midway up on the Spaceport Launch Tower during any major map condition, ideally the Hidden Bunker for extra farming time. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_12_02-46.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Launch Tower Location\"> From here, set up mines on entry points and utilize great sightlines to pull every Rocketeer on the map towards you. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_13_02-59.jpg\" alt=\"Setting Up at Launch Tower\"> Be aware, this is a high-traffic area, so players may attempt to engage in PvP.</li><li><strong>Farming Location 2: Blue Gate Pilgrim's Peak Tower</strong></li><li>Another excellent location is the tower at Pilgrim's Peak on Blue Gate. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_14_03-09.jpg\" alt=\"Pilgrim's Peak Tower Location\"> Bring a sniper and Wolfpacks to easily pull every Rocketeer on the map. This location also features a double Rocketeer spawn, meaning two quick kills with less resistance. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_16_03-22.jpg\" alt=\"Double Rocketeer Kill\"></li><li><strong>Targeting Rocketeers:</strong> Aim for the armor paneling over its central eye with heavy or energy ammo weapons. Breaking this panel exposes its crit spot, allowing for quick takedowns with regular gunfire. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_17_03-29.jpg\" alt=\"Rocketeer Weak Point\"></li></ul><h2>Step 2: Download Data During Hidden Bunker</h2><p>This trial requires downloading data from terminals inside the Hidden Bunker. We strongly recommend doing this solo due to the nature of the lobbies, but it takes a significant amount of time to complete. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_19_03-44.jpg\" alt=\"Entering the Hidden Bunker Map\"></p><ul><li>There are only 8 terminals inside the Hidden Bunker, each awarding 800 points per download. You need five terminals to reach the three-star ranking. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_21_04-02.jpg\" alt=\"Points for Data Download\"></li><li><strong>Activating the Bunker:</strong> When you load into the Hidden Bunker map, four antennas need to be activated before the bunker opens. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_23_04-16.jpg\" alt=\"Activating a Bunker Antenna\"> These antennas are randomly placed at the start of the map. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_25_04-31.jpg\" alt=\"Activating Third Antenna\"></li><li><strong>Entering the Bunker:</strong> Once all antennas are active, head to the bunker entrance. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_26_04-37.jpg\" alt=\"Bunker Entrance Open\"></li><li><strong>Downloading Data:</strong> Inside, find the eight computer terminals. Activate a terminal to begin downloading data. A yellow light will flash, and a green progress bar will appear. Once the bar completes, the light turns green, and data can be collected.</li><li><strong>Strategic Data Collection:</strong> Pay attention to which consoles are near completion and grab the data if you can. Move on to the next activated console rather than activating a new one yourself if other players are present, as you'll be stuck there during the download. Be cautious, as players can get impatient and attempt to use grenades. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_30_05-21.jpg\" alt=\"PvP at Terminals Warning\"></li><li>If you download all eight terminals and successfully extract, you'll secure 6400 points. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_31_05-34.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden Bunker Challenge Complete\"></li></ul><h2>Step 3: Search First Wave Husks</h2><p>Searching First Wave Husks is a straightforward challenge with high point farming potential. Each husk awards around 800 points.</p><ul><li>Look for dead ARC bodies (Rocketter husks, Baron husks, Hornet husks) that you can breach and loot throughout the environment. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_33_05-49.jpg\" alt=\"Points for Searching Husks\"> You can either be the one to breach them or simply interact with ones already breached by other players. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_36_06-06.jpg\" alt=\"Inventory Loot from Husks\"></li><li><strong>Optimal Location: Spaceport</strong></li><li>Spaceport is probably the best option due to the high number of husks that spawn on the outskirts of the map, away from typical danger zones. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_37_06-16.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Husk Locations\"> These areas rarely see PvP action. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_38_06-20.jpg\" alt=\"Farming Husks on Map Outskirts\"></li><li>This challenge is free loadout friendly, but bringing adrenaline shots is recommended to manage running across the map more efficiently. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_39_06-35.jpg\" alt=\"Crafting Adrenaline Shots\"></li></ul><h2>Step 4: Damage Snitches</h2><p>Damaging Snitches offers huge point farming potential because they respawn quickly once killed.</p><ul><li>Each Snitch awards 600 points, so you only need seven to achieve your three-star ranking for the week. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_41_06-50.jpg\" alt=\"Points for Damaging Snitches\"></li><li><strong>Elevated Strategy:</strong> Get yourself or your team to an elevated, centralized location on the map. Use a sniper or Jupiter to pull every Snitch to you. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_42_06-56.jpg\" alt=\"Elevated Snitch Farming Spot\"></li><li><strong>Map Conditions:</strong> Hidden Bunker offers extra time, making it a prime location. Night Raid and any other 2x condition on any map will also work. The key is elevation, the ability to defend that elevation from other teams, and suitable gear to quickly pull and take down ARC enemies. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_44_07-03.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden Bunker for Snitch Farming\"> <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_45_07-09.jpg\" alt=\"Night Raid for Snitch Farming\"> <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_47_07-18.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging Distant Snitch\"></li></ul><h2>Step 5: Damage Ground-Based ARC Enemies</h2><p>While this challenge has high point farming potential, it's often the hardest to achieve a high score due to contested enemies. You'll only receive 80% of the total XP gained on kills as points, meaning smaller enemies like Picks, Pops, and Fireballs yield very few points. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_49_07-26.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging Small ARC Enemies\"></p><ul><li><strong>Focus on Larger Enemies:</strong> Target larger enemies such as Bastions, Bombardiers, and Leapers, as these are ideal for farming points. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_51_07-51.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging a Leaper\"> <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_54_07-47.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging a Bastion\"></li><li><strong>Optimal Location: Hidden Bunker</strong></li><li>Hidden Bunker remains the best place to complete this challenge. Leapers, Bastions, and Bombardiers will spawn above the Hidden Bunker in a centralized location, and you'll have an extra 10 minutes to farm. Be aware, this will be a PvP hot zone. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_51_07-51.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging a Leaper\"> <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_56_07-58.jpg\" alt=\"Farming Leapers at Hidden Bunker\"></li><li><strong>Alternative Location: Dam Battlegrounds (Electromagnetic Storm)</strong></li><li>Dam Battlegrounds during an Electromagnetic Storm is another ideal map. It features two Bastion spawns, a Bombardier spawn, and three to five Leaper spawns. This gives solo players more options to avoid PvP, and groups can split up to maximize farming efforts. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_58_08-09.jpg\" alt=\"Dam Battlegrounds for Ground-Based Enemies\"> <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-5_59_08-13.jpg\" alt=\"Dam Battlegrounds Spawn Locations\"></li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide provides an in-depth breakdown of all the Week 5 competitive trial challenges, offering strategies, recommended gear, and optimal locations to efficiently earn maximum points and climb the leaderboards.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://img.youtube.com/vi/Vnj9nwDNKHQ/maxresdefault.jpg",
    "author": "All4nDev",
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-11-26T14:44:16.833556+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "74f6022e-c43f-48a8-895e-4dd87a8c9388",
    "title": "Trials Week 6 High Scoring Guide",
    "slug": "trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide",
    "content": "<h2>Overview: Weekly Trials &amp; General Tips</h2><p>This week's trials offer great potential for high scores, with the possibility of reaching 150,000 to 200,000 points. The guide will detail strategies for solo completion to achieve three stars, identifying the best point-farming opportunities, and suggesting free loadout-friendly options.</p><ul><li><strong>Major Map Conditions for Full Points:</strong> Only specific conditions yield full points: Hidden Bunker, Night Raids, and Electromagnetic Storms. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_6_00-53.jpg\" alt=\"Map Conditions for Trials\"> Minor conditions like Harvesters or Matriarchs only grant half points.</li><li><strong>Optimal Playstyle:</strong> For achieving three stars, playing solo is often easier due to fewer player interactions. However, for maximum leaderboard points, playing in a group of three is recommended. [SCREENSHOT:01:15]</li><li><strong>Hidden Bunker Map:</strong> While less reliant this week, the Hidden Bunker condition still offers the best environment for several trials.</li></ul><h2>Step 1: Damage Hornets</h2><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_12_01-49.jpg\" alt=\"Damage Hornets Overview\"></p><ul><li><strong>Points:</strong> 365 points per thruster kill, 760 points per main body kill. High farm potential, but not ideal for free loadouts.</li><li><strong>Recommended Farm Location:</strong> Spaceport, specifically the Trench Towers (South or North). <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_13_02-00.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Trench Towers Map\"></li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Drop into a Hidden Bunker map condition.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Use Adrenaline Shots to quickly reach one of the Trench Towers. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_14_02-07.jpg\" alt=\"Ziplining to Tower\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Zipline onto the tower.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Deploy Barricades and Traps around your position. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_15_02-26.jpg\" alt=\"Deploying Shield Recharger\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ensure weapons are well-repaired and bring plenty of ammo.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This high ground position offers excellent safety from other players and consistent Hornet spawns. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_16_02-49.jpg\" alt=\"Shooting Hornet from Tower\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Respawn Optimization:</strong> Kill all wasps and hornets in a patrol to encourage faster respawns of new patrols. If only hornets are killed, wasps remaining might delay new spawns.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Maximize Points:</strong> Aim for the main body of the Hornet (760 points) instead of just the thrusters (365 points) for higher scores. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_20_04-03.jpg\" alt=\"Hornet Main Body Hit\"></li><li>By following this method, players can realistically achieve upwards of 48,000 points in this trial. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_21_04-19.jpg\" alt=\"Damage Hornets Trial Result\"></li></ul><h2>Step 2: Deliver Carriables</h2><ul><li><br></li><li><br></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Points:</strong> 1000 points per carriable delivered. Bad farm potential, but great for free loadouts.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Recommended Maps:</strong> Spaceport or Dam Battlegrounds for the highest potential Field Crate spawns. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_23_05-05.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Field Depot Locations\"></li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Utilize an online interactive map to track potential Field Crate spawns. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_24_05-10.jpg\" alt=\"Interactive Spaceport Map\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Expect around 10 Field Crates per game at best.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Be aware of other players also doing this challenge, as they can clear spawns. [SCREENSHOT:05:35]</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">For a solo three-star completion, it's manageable, but for leaderboard farming, it requires many attempts and good RNG due to competition.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Focus on getting the three stars and don't over-invest if other players are active. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_25_05-24.jpg\" alt=\"Delivering Field Crate to Drop-off\"></li></ul><h2>Step 3: Damage Rocketeers, Leapers or Bastions</h2><ul><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_28_06-05.jpg\" alt=\"Damage Rocketeers, Leapers or Bastions Overview\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Points:</strong> Approximately 2,200 points per kill (tested on leapers &amp; rocketeers). Great farm potential, but bad for free loadouts.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Recommended Location:</strong> Spaceport, specifically the bottom of the Launch Towers. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_31_06-38.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Launch Towers Map\"></li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">This is an aggressive position, so be prepared for PvP encounters. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_32_06-48.jpg\" alt=\"Shooting Pop from Launch Tower\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">From the Launch Tower, you can spot 2-3 Leaper spawns, 3 Rocketeer spawns, and even a Bastion spawn. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_33_06-55.jpg\" alt=\"Launch Tower Vantage Point\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><strong>Hidden Bunker Alternative:</strong> The Hidden Bunker map also works for extra time, but beware of Bombardiers in the same areas as Bastions, which can be problematic. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_34_07-08.jpg\" alt=\"Engaging from Cover\"></li></ul><h2>Step 4: Destroy Pops</h2><ul><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_35_07-22.jpg\" alt=\"Destroy Pops Overview\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><strong>Points:</strong> 880 points per kill. Great farm potential, great for free loadouts (just needs loot ammo).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><strong>Recommended Location:</strong> Stella Montis, particularly during a Night Raid map condition. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_37_07-44.jpg\" alt=\"Shooting Pop Through Window\"></li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-4\">Queue for Stella Montis - Night Raid when it's nearing its final minutes or seconds. This can lead to a game that won't respawn new players, creating a quieter lobby for solo farming. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_39_08-08.jpg\" alt=\"Lobby Screen - Night Raid Queue\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-4\">Remain quiet in the initial minutes to allow other players to fight or extract, shrinking the lobby.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-4\">Once the lobby is smaller, rotate between the two sandbox areas, control areas, and the Metro Station extraction point, as Pops respawn quickly in these areas. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_40_08-20.jpg\" alt=\"High Ground Pop Engagement\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-4\"><strong>Alternative:</strong> If Stella Montis isn't ideal, Buried City is your second-best option. Focus on Research, Space Travel, Parking Garage, Hospital, and extraction points. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_43_09-25.jpg\" alt=\"Buried City Map\"></li></ul><h2>Step 5: Open ARC Probes</h2><ul><li><br></li><li><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_44_09-36.jpg\" alt=\"Open ARC Probes Overview\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-4\"><strong>Points:</strong> 1,334 points per search. Extremely free loadout friendly, great farm potential.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-4\"><strong>Recommended Map:</strong> Dam Battlegrounds on an Electromagnetic Storm. [SCREENSHOT:09:59]</li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-5\">Bring a lot of Adrenaline Shots to quickly cover the map.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-5\">In Electromagnetic Storms, probes often spawn in packs of two or three. [SCREENSHOT:10:07]</li><li class=\"ql-indent-5\">You don't need an interactive map; simply pay attention to the dark smoke coming from breached ARCs and constantly open your map.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-5\">ARC probes will show up on your map when you zoom in, even if they're far away. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_46_10-20.jpg\" alt=\"ARC Probes on Map\"></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Important:</strong> It's about 'searching' the probe, not 'breaching' it. If another player has already breached a probe, you can still search it for points. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-6-high-scoring-guide_47_10-27.jpg\" alt=\"Searching Breached Probe\"></li></ul>",
    "summary": "This guide covers how to efficiently complete the current weekly trials and specific farming methods for each challenge to maximize your earned points.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://img.youtube.com/vi/Laanx0LFgdY/maxresdefault.jpg",
    "author": "All4nDev",
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-12-03T06:50:01.661776+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "d43eb4c0-61c4-4b58-ae5f-ca44aef8c668",
    "title": "Trials Week 7",
    "slug": "trials-week-7",
    "content": "<h2>Overview: Weekly Trials Week 7</h2><p>This week marks the final week for Trials in Season 1, extending until Tuesday, offering players an extra day to complete objectives. The primary focus for many will be maintaining their current rank, though pushing for higher ranks is still possible. For maximum points, prioritize trials within major map conditions like Night Raids or Electromagnetic Storms, which grant double points. Queen/Matriarch trials, however, should be tackled in their specific minor map conditions (Harvester or Matriarch events).</p><h2>Destroy Ticks, Fireballs, and Pops</h2><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_5_02-41.jpg\" alt=\"Destroy Ticks, Fireballs, and Pops - Best Map\"></span></p><ul><li>Each kill grants 470 points.</li><li>The best map for this challenge is Stella Montis, specifically during a Night Raid event.</li><li>Stella Montis is densely populated with Ticks, Pops, and Fireballs.</li><li><strong>Strategic Queuing:</strong> Queue for a Night Raid on Stella Montis when it's nearing its final seconds or minutes. This can lead to an empty lobby with no mid-raid player respawns, allowing you to clear ARCs solo without PvP interference. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_6_03-09.jpg\" alt=\"Night Raid Queuing Strategy\"></span></li><li><strong>Recommended Locations:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Seed Vault has about 6-8 Ticks. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_7_03-57.jpg\" alt=\"Seed Vault Location\"></span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"> Archives is rich with Pops, Fireballs, and mini Ticks, particularly on the ceiling. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_8_04-10.jpg\" alt=\"Cochore Archives\"></span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\">The Control Rooms are also excellent spots for Pops and Fireballs. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_9_04-20.jpg\" alt=\"Sandboxes &amp; Control Rooms\"></span></li><li><strong>PvP Avoidance:</strong> Avoid high PvP areas like the Lobby, Medical Research, and Loading Bay. If you hear gunshots, change direction. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_10_04-43.jpg\" alt=\"High PvP Areas to Avoid\"></span> Once the lobby starts to clear up, you can extend your search. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_11_05-01.jpg\" alt=\"Late Game Lobby Clearing\"></span></li></ul><h2>Search Supply Drops</h2><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Each Supply Pod searched grants 1600 points.</li><li>This trial is highly RNG-dependent; there isn't one definitive best map. Spaceport has historically been consistent, though the video demonstrates a run on Dam Battlegrounds.</li><li><strong>Identifying Supply Stations:</strong> Look for a glowing white bulb shining on top of the station to indicate it hasn't been used yet. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_14_05-40.jpg\" alt=\"Identifying Supply Stations\"></span></li><li><strong>Gaining Points:</strong> You only need to 'tap' (loot) the supply pod to gain points; you don't need to call it in yourself. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_15_06-12.jpg\" alt=\"Looting a Supply Pod\"></span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\">Our interactive map can show potential spawn locations for them</span></li></ul><h2>Damage Wasps</h2><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_17_06-36.jpg\" alt=\"Damage Wasps - Best Map\"></span></p><ul><li>Each Wasp main body kill grants ~440 points.</li><li>The ideal location is Hidden Bunker when it's activated, as it spawns Wasps.</li><li>Alternatively, Spaceport during a Night Raid or Electromagnetic Storm event is a strong choice, focusing on the Launch Tower or Control Tower areas. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_18_06-45.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Zones for Wasps\"></span></li><li><strong>Strategy with Snitch Scanners:</strong> Hoard multiple Snitch Scanners, then position yourself on a high vantage point like the top of a tower on Spaceport. Deploy traps at entrances and use scanners to detect and eliminate Wasps as they appear. This is highly consistent for points.</li><li><strong>Strategy without Scanners:</strong> Take high ground (e.g., a tower), use traps to protect yourself, and attract Snitches. Snitches will call in two extra Wasps per reinforcement, helping you meet the ~10 Wasps needed for three stars. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_20_07-39.jpg\" alt=\"Wasp Farming without Scanners\"></span></li></ul><h2>Damage Bastions</h2><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_21_08-10.jpg\" alt=\"Damage Bastions - Spaceport Strategy\"></span></p><ul><li>Each Bastion kill grants ~4510 points.</li><li>Hidden Bunker, if active, is ideal as it spawns two Bastions directly on top, allowing for continuous farming. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_24_09-30.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden Bunker for Bastions\"></span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\">Spaceport is also an excellent choice, with a solid six potential spawn locations, typically guaranteeing two Bastions per game. You can rotate between kills and allowing them to respawn.</span></li><li><strong>Easy 3-Star Method:</strong> Bring 2-3 Wolfpacks; throwing them at a Bastion will instantly kill it, allowing for a quick extraction. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_23_09-20.jpg\" alt=\"Bastion Quick Kill with Wolfpacks\"></span></li><li><strong>Farming Strategy (Spaceport):</strong> For sustained point farming, either sit on top of Trench Tower and kill the Bastion below it or bunker up on Container Storage. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_22_08-44.jpg\" alt=\"Container Storage Bunker Spot\"></span> Be mindful of PvP, as heavy weapons like the Hullcracker attract attention.</li><li>If aiming for 3 stars without min-maxing, two Bastion kills are sufficient for over 8,000 points.</li></ul><h2>Damage Queens or Matriarchs</h2><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_25_10-06.jpg\" alt=\"Damage Queens/Matriarchs - Team Strategy\"></span></p><ul><li>Damage dealt translates to points at a 0.7:1 ratio. You need 5715 damage (not XP) to reach the 3-star threshold. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_26_10-28.jpg\" alt=\"Damage Threshold for 3 Stars\"></span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\">This is the most challenging and expensive trial for solo players.</span></li><li><strong>Method 1 (High Cost, Low Effort):</strong> Use approximately eight Wolfpacks. Each Wolfpack deals around 750 damage, totaling ~6000 damage, easily exceeding the 3-star requirement. This is costly but effective. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_27_11-25.jpg\" alt=\"Wolfpack Damage Calculation\"></span></li><li><strong>Method 2 (Risky):</strong> Get on top of the Queen/Matriarch and place Deadline mines. This can deal significant damage but is highly dangerous. <span style=\"background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); color: rgb(231, 233, 234);\"><img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/trials-week-7_28_11-55.jpg\" alt=\"Deadline Mine Strategy\"></span></li><li><strong>Method 3 (Recommended):</strong> Use a Jupiter instead of a Hullcracker. The Jupiter deals significantly more damage per shot and its ammo is cheaper to craft/buy. This method allows for faster damage accumulation.</li><li><strong>Safe Positioning:</strong> When engaging the Queen/Matriarch, find high ground or cover.</li><li><strong>Group Play:</strong> This trial is best completed in a trio. If other teams join the fight, they will steal damage points from you, making it harder to reach the 3-star threshold. Coordinate with your team to deal the damage and secure the kill entirely for yourselves.</li></ul>",
    "summary": null,
    "thumbnail_url": "https://img.youtube.com/vi/6zW1klusyZ8/maxresdefault.jpg",
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2025-12-08T11:11:08.315745+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "52e0a5df-6965-4e02-9a9b-8222f3611a2a",
    "title": "Turnabout",
    "slug": "turnabout",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>The 'Turnabout' quest requires you to obtain the Spaceport Trench Tower Key, navigate to the North Trench Tower, locate and upload the blackmail files to Celeste, and then successfully extract from the area.</p><h2>Step 1: Prepare Your Loadout</h2><ul><li>Ensure you have equipped an augment that includes at least one safe pocket in your loadout. [SCREENSHOT:00:15]</li><li>Place the 'Spaceport Trench Tower Key' (provided by the quest) into your safe pocket for safekeeping. </li><li>Note: If you happen to lose the key, you can find replacements by looting containers like drawers, cupboards, and lockers across any map.</li></ul><h2>Step 2: Navigate to North Trench Tower</h2><ul><li>Once spawned into Spaceport, open your map and pinpoint the 'North Trench Tower' located in the far northeast section of the map.</li><li>While the quest key can open either the North or South Trench Tower, your objective specifically requires entry into the North Trench Tower.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Enter the Tower</h2><ul><li>Approach the North Trench Tower from 'The Trench' area.</li><li>Locate the external stairs leading up to an underground floor entrance. Climb these stairs.</li><li>Proceed through the underground section, going up internal stairs to reach the surface level of the tower.</li><li>On the surface, find one of the two main doors. Interact to unlock and open it. </li></ul><h2>Step 4: Upload Blackmail Files</h2><ul><li>Once inside the tower, navigate through the first floor. There aren't any key objectives here, but you can search breach boxes for loot.</li><li>Find and climb the stairs leading up to the second floor. </li><li>On the second floor, locate a computer station positioned in the center, on the northeastern side of the room.</li><li>Interact with the computer to upload the blackmail files.</li></ul><h2>Step 5: Extract and Claim Rewards</h2><ul><li>After uploading the files, all that remains is to successfully extract from the mission area.</li><li>Return to Celeste at your base to hand in the quest and claim your rewards.</li></ul><p><br></p>",
    "summary": null,
    "thumbnail_url": null,
    "author": null,
    "type": "general",
    "objectives": [],
    "xp": 0,
    "rewards": [],
    "video_url": null,
    "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:19:55.89209+00:00"
  },
  {
    "id": "245331a0-83a6-4925-8a6c-37a4d2c1cd2b",
    "title": "Weekly Trials Nov 17th",
    "slug": "weekly-trials-nov-17th",
    "content": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>This guide covers tips for excelling in the weekly trials from November 17th to 23rd, focusing on specific objectives like harvesting plants, opening ARC probes, damaging flying ARC enemies, and damaging leapers. Pay attention to major map conditions for 2x points to maximize your score.</p><p><br></p><p>Used <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-YAQ09HcUno\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">this video</a> by Ebontis to make this guide</p><h2>Step 1: Harvest Plants</h2><p>For the 'Harvest Plants' trial, you need to harvest specific plant types like mushrooms, Great Mullein, or moss that have a fill-up bar, not just regular pickups.</p><ul><li>Mushrooms are generally unreliable to find.</li><li>Some moss can be found in the Hydroponic Dome Complex in Dam Battlegrounds.</li><li>**Best location:** Buried City, specifically the Galleria on a Night Raid condition. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_1_01-45.jpg\" alt=\"Buried City Galleria Location\"></li><li>You'll find numerous Great Mullein plants in planters and lobbies, offering about 500 points each (approximately 26-30 per run).</li></ul><h2>Step 2: Open ARC Probes</h2><p>For the 'Open ARC Probes' trial, you'll want to target probes with a ring around them that require interaction to open. ARC Couriers typically do not count.</p><ul><li>Choose larger maps with 2x point conditions, such as Hidden Bunker, to get more time (40 minutes instead of 30). <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_2_02-59.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden Bunker Map Condition\"></li><li>Each probe is worth around 1334 points, so opening three on a Night Raid will typically secure your 4000 points.</li><li>You can get lucky with multiple probes spawning close together, like the example of three probes near the Breach on Dam Battlegrounds during an Electromagnetic Storm.</li><li>To open a probe, you need to breach it open and then search the container.</li></ul><h2>Step 3: Damage Flying ARC Enemies</h2><p>This broad trial includes various flying enemies like Wasps, Spotters, Snitches, Hornets, and Rocketeers.</p><ul><li>For efficiency, consider using a **Hullcracker** (launcher weapon) as it has very strong ARC armor penetration. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_4_05-19.jpg\" alt=\"Hullcracker Weapon for Flying Enemies\"></li><li>The Hullcracker costs 30,000 currency and can be purchased once every 24 hours. Stock up on Launcher Ammo.</li><li>When targeting Rocketeers, focus fire on one side to disable two engines quickly, bringing them down.</li><li>Use **Snitch Scanners** to call in more enemies, including flying ones, to increase your damage output and points. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_6_07-09.jpg\" alt=\"Snitch Scanner for Enemy Spawns\"></li><li>Hullcracker can often one-shot Wasps and Hornets.</li></ul><h2>Step 4: Damage Leapers</h2><p>Leapers are vulnerable to fire damage.</p><ul><li>Utilize **Blaze Grenades** to set the ground on fire when Leapers jump at you or are stationary. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_7_08-09.jpg\" alt=\"Blaze Grenade for Leapers\"></li><li>**Fireball Burners** (from Fireballs) can also be effective.</li><li>The **Snap Blast Grenade** is recommended because it sticks to enemies, making it easier to deal consistent damage. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_8_09-05.jpg\" alt=\"Snap Blast Grenade for Leapers\"></li><li>The **Heavy Fuse Grenade** is an alternative but less reliable due to Leapers' movement. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_9_09-09.jpg\" alt=\"Heavy Fuse Grenade (Alternative)\"></li><li>The **Deadline mine** is highly effective if you can attach it to a Leaper, dealing a significant amount of damage. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_10_09-18.jpg\" alt=\"Deadline Mine for Leapers\"></li><li>Try running missions with an Electromagnetic Storm condition, as Leapers seem to be more common.</li><li>Hidden Bunker missions offer longer time (40 minutes) to find and defeat Leapers.</li></ul><h2>Step 5: Damage Queens or Matriarchs</h2><p>This trial requires you to damage either Queens or Matriarchs, which typically appear as specific map conditions.</p><ul><li>Currently, no Queen or Matriarch missions are active, but keep an eye out for them in areas like Spaceport or Hidden Bunker. <img src=\"https://iiugcpaznnwcegwificd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/guides/screenshots/weekly-trials-nov-17th_11_09-45.jpg\" alt=\"Spaceport Map for Bosses\"></li></ul><p><br></p>",
